window.DBD_DATA.perks.push(...[{"id":"flashbang","rank":37,"tier":"A","roles":["Team Support","Chase","Utility"],"summary":"Personal generator repair progress charges a craftable Flash Grenade that can blind the Killer and enable repeated pickup saves.","metaStatus":"Strong","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":5,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["pressure","bodyblock"],"useCases":["Create pickup saves without needing to bring a Flashlight into the Trial.","Use the grenade at pallets, windows, and confined paths to blind or disorient the Killer.","Recharge the perk through additional personal generator repair and craft multiple grenades in one Trial."],"counters":["Requires 40% personal generator repair progress at Tier III before each craft.","Pickup saves demand precise timing, position, and knowledge of Killer facing.","Poorly placed grenades can waste the charge without producing meaningful distance."],"pros":["Can be used multiple times when enough generator progress is earned.","Creates a save tool without consuming the Item slot.","High-skill users can turn one crafted grenade into a complete denial of a Killer pickup."],"cons":["High execution requirement for consistent saves.","Requires personal repair progress before each activation cycle.","Can encourage low-percentage rescue attempts that cost generator pressure."],"analysis":["Flashbang closes the top forty because its ceiling is much higher than its community tier label suggests, but that ceiling is execution-heavy. After enough personal generator progress, the Survivor can craft a grenade from a Locker and later use it to blind the Killer, including during pickup animations where a successful blind can erase a down entirely.","The perk's strongest trait is repeatability. Repairing more generators charges another craft, so a productive Survivor can generate several grenades during one Trial. Unlike a Flashlight, Flashbang also does not occupy the Item slot once crafted in the same way a dedicated carried tool shapes the loadout from the start.","Pickup saves are where the ranking becomes complicated. They require precise timing, good positioning, and often prediction about the Killer's facing and movement. Background Player helps solve the distance problem, while Head On and Quick & Quiet create additional Locker-centered play. In SWF, communication makes all of those save setups much easier to coordinate.","Flashbang stays at this position because many players will get less consistent value from it than from passive information or healing perks. A failed grenade does nothing, and chasing hero saves can harm team tempo. But a practiced player can turn generator participation into repeated opportunities to deny hooks, which is too impactful to rank as merely a novelty."],"verdict":"A high-skill utility perk with genuine hook-denial potential. Flashbang is inconsistent in casual hands, but repeated successful pickup saves can swing matches hard.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Save","Blind"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Leon S. Kennedy"},"synergyPerkIds":["background-player","head-on","quick-quiet","champion-of-light"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Background Player","Head On","Quick & Quiet","Champion of Light"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Flashbang","alternateName":null,"source":"Leon S. Kennedy","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After you contribute 50/45/40% total Generator repair progress, Flashbang activates. While hiding in a Locker, press the Active Ability button to craft a Flash Grenade; Flashbang deactivates after crafting. Further personal Generator repair progress charges it again, so it can be used multiple times in a Trial.","activation":["You must personally contribute the tier's total repair progress on Generators.","To craft the grenade, you must be hiding inside a Locker and press the Active Ability button.","Ends/deactivates when: Flashbang deactivates after the grenade is crafted."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.2.0): Reduced the total Generator repair requirement to 50/45/40% from 70/60/50%.","plainEnglishSummary":"Your Generator repair progress charges a Flash Grenade that you craft from inside a Locker.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Not token-based. After each crafting use, further personal Generator repair progress equal to the tier threshold charges another use.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"No once-per-Trial limit; one grenade is crafted per activation, with additional uses charged by further repair progress.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The charge comes from your own Generator repair contribution, not repair progress contributed by teammates."],"sourceCharacter":"Leon S. Kennedy","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"conviction","rank":38,"tier":"A","roles":["Anti-Slug","Recovery","Chase"],"summary":"After fully healing another Survivor, a future down can become a temporary self-pick once you reach 25% recovery, giving you up to 30 seconds before you collapse again.","metaStatus":"Strong","skillLevel":"Medium–High","soloQ":4,"swf":5,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["dying-state","anti-slug","broken"],"useCases":["Punish a Killer who leaves you slugged after you have already activated the perk by healing a teammate.","Stand yourself up long enough to reach safety, a pallet, a teammate, or a critical objective before the delayed collapse.","Force the Killer to decide whether to recommit to you instead of continuing a snowball."],"counters":["You must first complete a healing action on another Survivor.","You need at least 25% recovery while downed before the self-pick is available.","The recovery is temporary: you become Broken and automatically return to the Dying State after the duration."],"pros":["Can independently break a slugging sequence after a normal team-support action.","Creates a long temporary action window rather than merely adding recovery speed.","Strong SWF teams can plan around the delayed collapse and reposition you before it happens."],"cons":["Requires a prior teammate heal and a later slugging opportunity.","Does not permanently restore your health state by itself.","Can accomplish very little if the Killer immediately picks you up instead of leaving you down."],"analysis":["Conviction opens the this band band because it can create an enormous anti-slug swing, but only after several conditions line up. Completing a heal on another Survivor arms the perk. If you are later downed and left long enough to recover 25%, you can stand yourself back up and act for a substantial window before automatically collapsing again.","That temporary recovery should not be dismissed as fake value. Thirty seconds at Tier III can be enough to reach a distant pallet, crawl the strategic equivalent of an entire tile while standing, finish a rescue, reposition where a teammate can safely help, or simply force the Killer to abandon another target and deal with you. Any of those outcomes can disrupt a planned snowball.","The perk becomes much stronger in coordinated teams because the delayed collapse is predictable. Teammates can meet you at the end of the timer, create a protection route, or use Soul Guard and other recovery tools to complicate the Killer's response. Solo Q still gets meaningful independence, but random teammates are less likely to understand the timing.","Conviction remains outside the top forty because it is conditional in three separate ways: heal someone first, get downed later, and actually be slugged long enough to recover. Community ratings are extremely positive, but our ranking weights consistency as heavily as ceiling. When it activates in the right match, it can look far stronger than this position."],"verdict":"A high-ceiling anti-slug perk with real match-flipping potential. Conviction is held back by setup and opportunity frequency, not by the strength of a successful activation.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Michonne Grimes"},"synergyPerkIds":["soul-guard","unbreakable","plot-twist","were-gonna-live-forever"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Soul Guard","Unbreakable","Plot Twist","We're Gonna Live Forever"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Conviction","alternateName":null,"source":"Michonne Grimes","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After completing a healing action on another Survivor, while in the Dying State and after recovering at least 25%, use the Active Ability button to recover fully. You then suffer Broken and return to the Dying State after 20/25/30 seconds.","activation":["Complete a healing action on another Survivor.","Be in Dying State with at least 25% recovery progress.","Use Active Ability.","Ends/deactivates when: Returns you to Dying after 20/25/30 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.3.0): Changed the prerequisite to healing another Survivor to prevent an interaction with Plot Twist.","plainEnglishSummary":"Completing a heal lets you stand up once from the Dying State before becoming Broken and going back down after a delay.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Delayed return to Dying: 20/25/30 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Broken"],"specialInteractions":["Requires completed healing of another Survivor; incomplete healing does not qualify."],"sourceCharacter":"Michonne Grimes","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"desperate-measures","rank":39,"tier":"A","roles":["Healing","Rescue","Utility"],"summary":"For each injured, dying, or hooked Survivor, heal and unhook 20% faster at Tier III, scaling up to an 80% bonus.","metaStatus":"Strong","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":4,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["reset","dying-state","hook-state","health-state"],"useCases":["Speed up emergency heals when several teammates are injured.","Create extremely fast unhooks during snowball pressure.","Exploit the perk's strongest stacks exactly when the team is in danger."],"counters":["Low bonus when the team is healthy.","Does not help generator repair.","The highest stacks usually occur in dangerous game states where reaching the action can still be difficult."],"pros":["Excellent comeback scaling.","Affects both healing and unhooking.","No cooldown or activation button."],"cons":["Weakest when the team is already stable.","Can look better numerically than it feels if the Killer controls access to the hook or downed players.","No direct chase benefit."],"analysis":["Desperate Measures earns its place because its strongest numbers arrive exactly when Survivors most need speed. One injured teammate gives a useful bonus; two or three injured, downed, or hooked teammates can make healing and unhooking dramatically faster.","The perk is especially strong during snowballs. A normal heal may be too slow before the Killer returns, while a heavily stacked Desperate Measures can create a reset window that otherwise would not exist. The same scaling can make contested unhooks much harder to interrupt.","It is also one of the easiest support perks to use. There is no token economy or special trigger beyond the team's current health states. If the match is messy, the perk is strong automatically.","The downside is that it is inherently reactive. A healthy team gets little value, and the perk cannot create objective pressure on its own. Even so, its 9.0-era 20%-per-stack ceiling is too strong to leave buried in mid-B."],"verdict":"An excellent comeback support perk. Desperate Measures gets stronger as the match gets uglier, and its current 20%-per-stack scaling can rescue otherwise hopeless reset windows.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Comeback"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Felix Richter"},"synergyPerkIds":["botany-knowledge","well-make-it","were-gonna-live-forever","do-no-harm"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Botany Knowledge","We'll Make It","We're Gonna Live Forever","Do No Harm"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Desperate Measures","alternateName":null,"source":"Felix Richter","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"For each injured, Dying, or hooked Survivor (including you), increase Healing and Unhooking speed by 16/18/20%, up to four stacks (64/72/80%).","activation":["At least one Survivor is injured, Dying, or hooked; you are included.","Ends/deactivates when: Bonus decreases as qualifying Survivors return to Healthy or leave the qualifying state."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.0.0): Increased the per-Survivor bonus to 16/18/20%.","plainEnglishSummary":"Injured, downed, or hooked teammates increase your Healing and Unhooking speed.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Per qualifying Survivor: 16/18/20%; maximum 64/72/80%."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Stacks once per injured, Dying, or hooked Survivor, including you; max four stacks.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Felix Richter","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"dark-sense","rank":40,"tier":"A","roles":["Information","Chase","Utility"],"summary":"Each Generator completion arms a 13–15 second information burst that reveals the Killer, teammates, Pallets, and Windows when the Killer comes within 20 metres.","metaStatus":"Strong","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","pressure"],"useCases":["Receive an early warning when the Killer approaches after a generator completion.","Use the long Aura read to understand their direction through walls.","Bank the trigger until the Killer actually enters a relevant local range."],"counters":["Requires a generator to complete before each use.","Only triggers when the Killer comes within 20 metres.","Undetectable and Aura denial can suppress the key information."],"pros":["13/14/15-second Killer Aura is long.","Trigger waits for the Killer to approach rather than firing immediately at generator completion.","Simple and passive."],"cons":["One use per generator completion.","No benefit before the team makes objective progress.","Pure information."],"analysis":["Dark Sense is effectively a new perk in 10.2. When armed by a Generator completion and triggered by the Killer approaching within 20 metres, it reveals the Killer, all other Survivors, and nearby Pallets and Windows for up to fifteen seconds.","That is a huge amount of information in one window. Newer players receive the map-learning utility that old Windows of Opportunity used to provide, while experienced players can use the Killer Aura and teammate positions to make precise chase and rotation decisions.","The activation is not permanent. A Generator must complete first, and the information waits until the Killer enters local range, so a quiet portion of the match can still pass without value.","The 10.1 ranking is no longer meaningful. Dark Sense moved from a narrow Killer-warning perk into a broad, free general information package and should be reviewed much higher."],"verdict":"One of 10.2’s biggest Survivor information winners. Dark Sense now teaches resources, shows teammates, and tracks the Killer in the same long trigger window.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:audit-explicit"],"tags":["Beginner"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[32,55],"rankConfidence":"Low","rankStatus":"provisional","evidenceStatus":"needs-post-10.2-data","acquisition":{"type":"general","sourceCharacter":"General"},"synergyPerkIds":["eyes-of-belmont","alert","poised","deja-vu"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Eyes of Belmont","Alert","Poised","Déjà Vu"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Dark Sense","alternateName":null,"source":"General perk","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever a Generator is completed, Dark Sense activates. When the Killer comes within 20 metres of you, for 13/14/15 seconds you see the Killer's Aura, the Auras of other Survivors, and the Auras of Pallets and Windows within 32 metres. The perk then deactivates until another Generator is completed.","activation":["A Generator is completed.","While the perk is active, the Killer comes within 20 metres.","Ends/deactivates when: The Aura-reading window ends after 13/14/15 seconds and Dark Sense deactivates until another Generator is completed."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Reworked to trigger at 20 metres and reveal the Killer, other Survivors, and nearby Pallets/Windows for 13/14/15 seconds after a Generator completion arms the perk.","plainEnglishSummary":"Generator completion arms a multi-Aura information window that triggers when the Killer approaches within 20 metres.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Aura-reading window: 13/14/15 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Reactivates on each subsequent Generator completion.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["During the active window, reveals the Killer and other Survivors, plus Pallets and Windows within 32 metres."],"sourceCharacter":"General","isGeneralPerk":true,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"for-the-people","rank":41,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Rescue"],"summary":"While Healthy, instantly trade one of your Health States to heal another Survivor by one state, then become Injured and Broken.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["health-state","broken","dying-state"],"useCases":["Instantly pick a downed teammate back to Injured before the Killer can secure the pickup.","Turn an Injured teammate Healthy without spending normal healing time when immediate tempo matters.","Use coordinated health-state trades to deny a snowball or save a teammate on death hook."],"counters":["You must be Healthy and cannot perform the activation while using a Med-Kit.","You become Injured and Broken for up to 60 seconds at Tier III.","Poor timing can simply transfer the Killer's pressure from one vulnerable Survivor to another."],"pros":["Instant healing can deny a down or save several seconds at a critical moment.","Extremely strong in coordinated teams that know when the health-state trade is worth it.","Can change who the Killer is able to pressure immediately."],"cons":["Costs your own Healthy state.","Broken prevents an immediate reset afterward.","Solo Q teammates may not capitalize on the tempo you create."],"analysis":["For the People ranks this position because instant health-state transfers can produce some of the sharpest Survivor tempo swings outside a direct save perk. A teammate on the ground can be returned to Injured immediately, denying the Killer a comfortable pickup if the timing is right.","The perk is especially dangerous in SWF because the team can engineer the trade. A Healthy Survivor knows exactly when to step in, the recipient knows to move immediately, and the rest of the team can cover the now-Injured user. That coordination can turn one expected hook into two mobile Survivors.","The cost prevents the perk from ranking much higher. You do not create a free health state; you move one from yourself to someone else and accept Broken afterward. In a poor position, the Killer can simply hit the new Injured target or switch to you. The perk therefore rewards situational judgment more than raw button timing.","For the People is strongest when one Survivor's continued mobility matters more than your own Healthy state, such as protecting someone on death hook or breaking a slugging sequence. It is not an every-heal perk. Used sparingly, it is excellent; used casually, it can make the team easier to pressure."],"verdict":"An elite emergency health-state trade, not a routine heal. For the People is powerful because it changes timing instantly, but the user must know when sacrificing their own safety is actually worth it.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Tempo"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Zarina Kassir"},"synergyPerkIds":["were-gonna-live-forever","made-for-this","dead-hard","shoulder-the-burden"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["We're Gonna Live Forever","Made for This","Dead Hard","Shoulder the Burden"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"For the People","alternateName":null,"source":"Zarina Kassir","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While healthy and actively healing another Survivor without using a Med-Kit, press the Active Ability button to trade one Health State: a dying or Deep Wounded target is healed to Injured, while an injured target is healed to full health. You become injured and Broken for 80/70/60 seconds, and become the Killer's Obsession if you are not already. The perk reduces your chance of being the initial Obsession by 100%.","activation":["You must be healthy.","You must be healing another Survivor.","You must not be using a Med-Kit for that healing action.","Press the Active Ability button.","Ends/deactivates when: The active effect is consumed when used.","Ends/deactivates when: Broken lasts for 80/70/60 seconds; the healthy-state requirement also has to be met again before another use."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (5.3.0): Reduced the duration of the Broken status effect from 110/100/90 to 80/70/60 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"While healing someone, you can trade one of your Health States to heal theirs instantly, at the cost of becoming injured and Broken.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Self-inflicted Broken: 80/70/60 seconds (Tier I/II/III)."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"No fixed once-per-Trial limit; each use requires meeting the healthy and active-healing conditions again. The Killer can have only one Obsession at a time.","statusEffectsInvolved":["Broken","Deep Wound"],"specialInteractions":["A dying or Deep Wounded target is healed to Injured; an injured target is healed to full health.","Makes you the Killer's Obsession if you are not already, while reducing your chance of being the initial Obsession by 100%."],"sourceCharacter":"Zarina Kassir","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"dramaturgy","rank":42,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Exhaustion","Utility"],"summary":"While healthy, trigger a short Haste burst and roll one of four follow-up effects, ranging from another burst to a free Rare Item or temporary Exposed.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["haste","exhausted"],"useCases":["Create immediate distance during a chase without needing a vault, drop, or elevation trigger.","Fish for a second Haste burst when extra distance would break the Killer's pressure.","Generate additional Rare Items over the course of a Trial when the random roll cooperates."],"counters":["It only activates while Healthy and cannot be used while Exhausted.","The Exposed result can turn an otherwise safe health state into a dangerous one for 12 seconds.","The random secondary effect makes the perk less predictable than conventional Exhaustion perks.","Hex: Under Your Thumb can cap running Haste while the Hex remains lit."],"pros":["Activation is player-controlled while running and Healthy.","The guaranteed first Haste burst always provides some chase value.","The free-item result can create substantial extra utility beyond movement."],"cons":["Randomness can produce a scream or Exposed at a bad moment.","Cannot be activated while injured.","Less predictable than Sprint Burst, Lithe, or other deterministic chase perks."],"analysis":["Dramaturgy takes this position because the guaranteed part of the perk is already useful before considering the chaos attached to it. While Healthy, the Survivor can deliberately activate a 25% Haste burst for two seconds without needing a window, pallet, or drop. That makes the trigger unusually flexible for an Exhaustion perk.","The secondary roll is what gives Dramaturgy its strange ceiling. A second Haste instance can produce excellent chase distance, while the Rare Item roll can create real resource value for the rest of the Trial. The scream is usually a manageable downside, and Exposed is the dangerous outcome because it temporarily removes the protection normally provided by being Healthy.","The skill is therefore not mechanical execution so much as risk management. Activating while the Killer is already close enough to capitalize on Exposed can backfire, while using the perk at a transition or when a little extra distance reaches a strong tile reduces the danger. Experienced users also know when the chance of an item is worth the Exhaustion commitment.","It ranks below the most reliable chase perks because randomness is still randomness. Lithe, Sprint Burst, and Balanced Landing tell you exactly what they will do. Dramaturgy can occasionally exceed them, but it can also give you the least useful secondary result at the worst possible time. Its ceiling can be excellent, but its randomness prevents top-end dependability."],"verdict":"A strong, flexible Exhaustion perk with controlled activation and uncontrolled flavor. The guaranteed Haste is good; the random second effect determines whether the activation becomes merely useful or spectacular.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Nicolas Cage"},"synergyPerkIds":["vigil","resilience","built-to-last","botany-knowledge"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Vigil","Resilience","Built to Last","Botany Knowledge"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Dramaturgy","alternateName":null,"source":"Nicolas Cage","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"At full Health, while running use the Active Ability button to perform a 0.5-second animation and gain 25% Haste for 2 seconds. It then triggers one secondary effect, never the same one twice consecutively: another 25% Haste instance for 2 seconds, Exposed for 12 seconds, a scream, or a random Rare Item with random Add-ons (dropping your held Item). Cannot be used while Exhausted and causes Exhausted for 60/50/40 seconds.","activation":["Be at full Health.","Be running and not Exhausted when activating.","Ends/deactivates when: Haste lasts 2 seconds; Exposed lasts 12 seconds; item is granted immediately."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (7.1.0): Introduced; no later material live balance change located in the official notes checked.","plainEnglishSummary":"At full Health, use the ability while running for a short Haste burst and a random secondary effect.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Animation: 0.5 seconds.","Primary Haste: 2 seconds.","Possible Exposed: 12 seconds.","Exhausted: 60/50/40 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Haste","Exposed","Exhausted"],"specialInteractions":["Secondary effect is random and cannot repeat the immediately preceding secondary effect.","If an Item is granted, the Item you held is dropped."],"sourceCharacter":"Nicolas Cage","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"boon-circle-of-healing","rank":43,"tier":"B","roles":["Boon","Healing","Team Support"],"summary":"Create a 24-metre healing zone where Survivors heal teammates dramatically faster and can see injured allies.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["reset","aura-reading","health-state"],"useCases":["Create a team reset zone after several Survivors become injured.","Use injured-Survivor Aura reading inside the Boon area to coordinate heals without voice.","Stack the same blessed Totem with Shadow Step, Steadfast, or other Boon effects."],"counters":["Requires time to find and bless a Totem.","The Killer can snuff the Boon and remove the healing zone.","Survivors cannot self-heal from Circle of Healing alone in its current design."],"pros":["Can benefit the whole team rather than only the owner.","Up to 100% faster teammate healing is a major reset bonus.","Combines efficiently with other Boons on the same Totem."],"cons":["Location-dependent and vulnerable to snuffing.","Does not independently solve self-healing.","Repeated re-blessing can consume too much objective time."],"analysis":["Circle of Healing sits at this position because its modern identity is a team reset accelerator rather than the old self-healing powerhouse. Survivors inside the 24-metre zone heal other Survivors much faster and can see injured teammate Auras, making the Boon a clear rally point after pressure.","The strongest use is after multi-injury situations. Instead of several slow individual heals, the team can regroup in the zone and recover quickly. The Aura component also improves Solo Q usability because injured players become easy to locate once everyone reaches the area.","Boon stacking raises the ceiling considerably. Shadow Step can make the same zone harder for the Killer to track, while Steadfast can add generator value if the Totem covers a useful objective cluster. One setup action can therefore activate several team effects when the build is intentionally constructed around Boons.","The weaknesses are the usual Boon weaknesses: setup, geography, and snuffing. A poorly placed Totem may cover nothing useful, while an obvious one can be removed immediately. Circle of Healing is strong when the team uses the zone rather than treating the Boon itself as the objective."],"verdict":"A strong team-reset Boon in its current support-focused form. Circle of Healing is best when several Survivors actually use the zone, especially as part of a multi-Boon setup.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Team"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Mikaela Reid"},"synergyPerkIds":["boon-shadow-step","boon-steadfast","botany-knowledge","flow-state"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Boon: Shadow Step","Boon: Steadfast","Botany Knowledge","Flow State"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Boon: Circle of Healing","alternateName":null,"source":"Mikaela Reid","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Bless a Dull or Hex Totem to create a Boon Totem. Survivors within 24 metres hear its chimes, heal other Survivors 50/75/100% faster when not using a Med-Kit, and see injured Survivors' Auras.","activation":["Bless a Dull or Hex Totem.","Affected Survivors must be within 24 metres.","Healing bonus applies when healing another Survivor without a Med-Kit.","Ends/deactivates when: Effects end outside Boon range or when the totem is snuffed."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (6.7.0): Reworked to altruistic healing only (50/75/100%, not with Med-Kits) and added injured-Survivor Aura reading.","plainEnglishSummary":"A Boon Totem speeds altruistic healing without Med-Kits and reveals injured teammates nearby.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"A Survivor can maintain only one active Boon Totem; all equipped Boon perks apply to it.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Healing-speed bonus does not apply to Med-Kit healing.","Injured Survivor Auras are revealed to others within range."],"sourceCharacter":"Mikaela Reid","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"boon-steadfast","rank":44,"tier":"B","roles":["Boon","Objective"],"summary":"Create a 24-metre zone where generators repair faster, regress more slowly, and are revealed to Survivors in the area.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium–High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["pressure","aura-reading"],"useCases":["Anchor a contested generator cluster with a 10% repair-speed bonus at Tier III.","Reduce passive regression on generators the Killer repeatedly pushes Survivors away from.","Stack objective value with other Boon effects on one well-positioned Totem."],"counters":["Only generators inside the Boon radius receive the effects.","The Killer can snuff the Totem and erase the setup.","Bad Totem placement can leave the perk with no meaningful generator coverage."],"pros":["Teamwide 10% repair-speed increase inside the zone is substantial.","Also halves regression speed, helping contested objectives retain progress.","Generator Aura visibility helps teammates understand which objectives the Boon supports."],"cons":["Very dependent on Totem and generator geometry.","Requires setup before generating any objective value.","A Killer who notices the protected cluster can prioritize snuffing the Boon."],"analysis":["Boon: Steadfast takes this position because its effect is legitimately strong when the map gives it the right geometry. A generator inside the radius repairs 10% faster at Tier III and regresses 50% more slowly, while its Aura is visible to Survivors in the zone. That combines acceleration, retention, and information.","The 10% repair bonus is especially meaningful on a generator the team already wants to prioritize, such as a central objective or a dangerous cluster identified by Déjà Vu. Unlike Prove Thyself, the Boon can support different Survivors working at different times as long as the generator remains inside the area.","Its placement requirement is the entire ranking problem. A powerful Boon beside the wrong edge generator is not powerful in practice. The Survivor may also spend time searching for the ideal Totem only to have the Killer snuff it shortly afterward.","As a newly introduced 10.1 perk, Steadfast deserves caution rather than immediate top-tier enthusiasm. Early usage is meaningful and the effect is numerically strong, but map variance is unavoidable. In a good setup it can look better than this position; in a bad one it can struggle to justify the blessing time."],"verdict":"A strong objective Boon with a geometry tax. Steadfast can make a contested generator cluster much harder for the Killer to control, but only when a useful Totem actually covers it.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Anti-Regression"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Aurora Stardotter"},"synergyPerkIds":["deja-vu","boon-shadow-step","boon-circle-of-healing","prove-thyself"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Déjà Vu","Boon: Shadow Step","Boon: Circle of Healing","Prove Thyself"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Boon: Steadfast","alternateName":null,"source":"Aurora Stardotter","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Bless a Dull or Hex Totem. Survivors within 24 metres hear its chimes. Generators within the radius regress 50% more slowly; Survivors repair 8/9/10% faster. Generator Auras in the radius are revealed to Survivors there.","activation":["Bless a Dull or Hex Totem.","The Generator or Survivor must be within 24 metres for its relevant effect.","Ends/deactivates when: Effects end outside the radius or when the totem is snuffed."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.1.0): Introduced with 50% slower Generator regression and 8/9/10% faster repair.","plainEnglishSummary":"A Boon Totem reveals nearby Generators, slows their regression, and speeds nearby repairs.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"One active Boon Totem per Survivor; equipped Boons apply to that totem.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Generator Auras are revealed to Survivors in the Boon radius."],"sourceCharacter":"Aurora Stardotter","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"any-means-necessary","rank":45,"tier":"B","roles":["Pallet","Information","Objective"],"summary":"See dropped Pallets anywhere and restore one upright in 3 seconds at Tier III when the Killer leaves it unbroken.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["looping"],"useCases":["Recover strong pallets the Killer left dropped but unbroken.","Use dropped-pallet Auras as global information about where chases and resource use are happening.","Restore a pallet after a teammate is forced to leave the area, preserving a future chase resource."],"counters":["A Killer who breaks important pallets immediately denies the reset ability.","Resetting a weak pallet can waste time for little strategic gain.","Traveling across the map solely to recover a pallet can cost more objective time than the pallet is worth."],"pros":["Combines pallet-state information with actual resource restoration.","Only three seconds are needed for the Tier III reset interaction.","Excellent Solo Q awareness even when no pallet is worth resetting."],"cons":["Depends on the Killer leaving pallets intact.","Not all pallets are valuable enough to justify the detour.","Provides no direct benefit at untouched tiles."],"analysis":["Any Means Necessary earns this position because it quietly does two useful jobs. The Aura-reading portion tells you where pallets have been dropped, which acts as a global map of recent chase activity and resource consumption. The active portion then lets you restore a dropped pallet when the Killer chooses not to break it.","The information has value even if you never reset anything. Seeing several pallets go down on one side of the map tells you where pressure has been concentrated and which routes may be weaker later. In Solo Q, that fills an information gap teammates normally cannot communicate.","The three-second Tier III reset is fast enough to make opportunistic recovery practical. Strong Killers will usually break premium pallets, but greedier or power-dependent Killers sometimes leave them down. Recovering even one strong pallet can meaningfully extend a later chase.","It ranks below broader information perks because the Killer controls much of the opportunity. If every important pallet is destroyed, the active half disappears. Still, the combination of map knowledge and occasional resource restoration makes Any Means Necessary much more than a novelty."],"verdict":"A smart pallet-management perk with useful information even when no reset happens. Its ceiling depends on the Killer leaving resources behind, but one recovered strong pallet can matter a lot.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Resource"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Yui Kimura"},"synergyPerkIds":["chemical-trap","five-moves-ahead","lithe"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"synergies":["Chemical Trap","Five Moves Ahead","Lithe"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Any Means Necessary","alternateName":null,"source":"Yui Kimura","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"The Auras of dropped Pallets are revealed to you. While standing beside a dropped Pallet, hold the Active Ability button to reset it upright over 5/4/3 seconds.","activation":["Stand beside a dropped Pallet and hold the Active Ability button.","Ends/deactivates when: Reset interaction ends if interrupted."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.1.0): Reduced the reset interaction to 5/4/3 seconds from 6/5/4 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"You can see dropped Pallets and restore one upright by holding the ability button beside it.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Pallet reset interaction: 5/4/3 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Yui Kimura","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"reassurance","rank":46,"tier":"B","roles":["Rescue","Objective"],"summary":"From within 6 metres, pause a hooked Survivor's sacrifice timer for up to 30 seconds once per hook instance.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["hook-state","pressure","trade"],"useCases":["Buy generator time when the Killer is camping or heavily contesting a hook.","Pause a second-stage timer while the team organizes a safer rescue instead of forcing an immediate trade.","Stabilize endgame hooks where rushing the save would feed the Killer multiple downs."],"counters":["You must get within 6 metres of the hooked Survivor, which can itself be dangerous against a camping Killer.","It can be used only once per Survivor per Hook Instance.","If the team already has a safe immediate rescue, delaying the hook timer may add little practical value."],"pros":["Can turn camping into extra generator time instead of forcing a bad rescue.","Particularly strong in coordinated teams that know exactly how to use the extra 30 seconds.","Pausing Struggle Skill Checks reduces mechanical pressure while the timer is frozen."],"cons":["Very situational when the Killer leaves hooks normally.","The six-metre activation range can expose the user to hits or trades.","Solo Q teammates may not understand that the extra hook time is meant to be converted into objectives or a better rescue setup."],"analysis":["Reassurance closes this batch at this position because its best-case value is enormous but concentrated in a very specific problem: a Killer who is heavily defending the hook. In that situation, immediately forcing a rescue can be exactly what the Killer wants. Reassurance lets the team refuse that timing and create another 30 seconds of decision space.","Those 30 seconds matter because three other Survivors can convert them into generators, healing, positioning, or a coordinated rescue plan. The perk therefore does not merely save hook time; it changes the economic trade around camping. A Killer who continues to stand near the hook may be giving the rest of the team substantially more objective progress than they expected.","SWF gets the cleanest value because everyone can agree on what the pause means. One player uses Reassurance, others stay on generators, and the rescue happens later under better conditions. In Solo Q, some teammates will still panic and approach the hook immediately, reducing the perk's strategic payoff even though the timer itself is successfully paused.","The reason Reassurance does not rank higher is opportunity frequency. Many Killers leave the hook, and in those matches a normal rescue happens before the pause matters. It is therefore weaker as a blind general-purpose slot than Bond or Distortion. But when the match becomes hook-defense heavy, few perks buy time as directly or as safely for the team."],"verdict":"A high-impact anti-camp tool whose strength depends on the Killer giving you the problem it solves. In coordinated teams, 30 extra hook seconds can be converted into a brutal amount of objective time.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Anti-Camp","Time"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[40,60],"rankConfidence":"Medium","rankStatus":"stable","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Rebecca Chambers"},"synergyPerkIds":["kindred","shoulder-the-burden","well-make-it","background-player"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Kindred","Shoulder the Burden","We'll Make It","Background Player"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Reassurance","alternateName":null,"source":"Rebecca Chambers","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While within 6 metres of a hooked Survivor, press Active Ability to pause that Survivor's Sacrifice Process for 20/25/30 seconds. This also pauses Struggle Skill Checks if that Survivor is in the Struggle Phase, and highlights the hooked Survivor's outline in white to you. Reassurance can be used only once per Survivor per Hook Instance.","activation":["Be within 6 metres of a hooked Survivor and press Active Ability.","Ends/deactivates when: The pause and outline effects end after 20/25/30 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (6.2.0): Removed the 40-second cooldown and added the once-per-Survivor-per-Hook-Instance use limit.","plainEnglishSummary":"Near a hook, it pauses that Survivor's Sacrifice Process briefly and marks their outline for you.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Sacrifice Process pause and white outline: 20/25/30 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Once per Survivor per Hook Instance; a Hook Instance is a single continuous hook event, even if the Survivor advances from first to second Hook Stage without being unhooked.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["If the hooked Survivor is in the Struggle Phase, their Struggle Skill Checks are paused too.","One activation can affect multiple hooked Survivors within range when several are hooked close together, such as in the Basement."],"sourceCharacter":"Rebecca Chambers","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"spine-chill","rank":47,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Information"],"summary":"When the Killer looks at you within 40 metres, gain a warning plus 12 seconds of scream immunity and 10% faster vaults.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":4,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["pressure"],"useCases":["Get an early warning when the Killer is looking at you within range.","Convert the opening of a chase into a short window of faster vaults.","Suppress screams during the active window against scream-based effects."],"counters":["The effect is temporary and then enters a cooldown, so it cannot cover every vault in a chase.","An early trigger can waste part of the 12-second window before a decisive vault occurs.","Its exact post-10.2 chase conversion still needs live data."],"pros":["Combines warning, scream suppression, and chase-relevant vault speed.","Useful without teammate coordination.","Much more directly chase-oriented than its old action-speed identity."],"cons":["Cooldown limits uptime.","Warning value overlaps normal Killer awareness in many matchups.","Exact rank remains provisional until post-10.2 play data exists."],"analysis":["Spine Chill was rebuilt into a chase-warning perk in 10.2. The old broad action-speed package is gone; instead, a Killer looking at you within 40 metres triggers a notification, twelve seconds of scream immunity, and 10% faster vaulting.","The vault bonus is the important competitive piece. Ten percent can alter close Window timings, and the trigger naturally occurs as the Killer notices or approaches you rather than requiring a manual activation.","The effect has a 40/35/30-second cooldown, so it cannot be permanent chase insurance. It also no longer speeds generators, healing, gates, or the many other actions associated with historical Spine Chill.","Modern Spine Chill deserves a fresh chase-based evaluation. It is narrower than the old generalist version but more directly useful during the moment a Killer is committing attention to you."],"verdict":"A cleaner 10.2 chase perk: warning, scream immunity, and 10% faster vaults when the Killer looks your way. The old action-speed identity is gone.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:audit-explicit"],"tags":["Awareness","Vault"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[40,65],"rankConfidence":"Low","rankStatus":"provisional","evidenceStatus":"needs-post-10.2-data","acquisition":{"type":"general","sourceCharacter":"General"},"synergyPerkIds":["resilience","premonition","alert","wake-up"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Resilience","Premonition","Alert","Wake Up!"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Spine Chill","alternateName":null,"source":"General perk","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever the Killer looks at you within 40 metres, you are notified, cannot scream for 12 seconds, and vault 10% faster for 12 seconds. Cooldown: 40/35/30 seconds.","activation":["The Killer looks at you while within 40 metres.","The perk is not on cooldown.","Ends/deactivates when: The scream-prevention and vault-speed effects end after 12 seconds.","Ends/deactivates when: The perk cannot trigger again during its 40/35/30-second cooldown."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Complete rework: when the Killer looks at you within 40 metres, gain a notification, 12 seconds of scream prevention, and 10% faster vaulting, with a 40/35/30-second cooldown.","plainEnglishSummary":"A nearby Killer looking at you triggers a warning, temporary scream immunity, and faster vaulting.","cooldown":"40/35/30 seconds.","duration":["Cannot scream: 12 seconds.","Vault speed +10%: 12 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"General","isGeneralPerk":true,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"poised","rank":48,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Stealth","Objective"],"summary":"The first time you start repairing each Generator, reveal the Killer for 8 seconds; whenever a Generator completes, hide your Scratch Marks for up to 30 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","pressure","solo-q"],"useCases":["Use the first repair touch on a generator as an 8-second Killer location check.","Rotate safely after any generator completion with hidden Scratch Marks.","Combine objective play with passive information instead of sacrificing a slot to pure scouting."],"counters":["Each generator grants the Aura read only once.","Scratch-Mark suppression after completion matters only if movement and Killer proximity make it relevant.","Undetectable or Aura-blocking effects can reduce the information value."],"pros":["Strong passive value from normal objective play.","Eight-second Aura reads are long enough to guide real decisions.","Thirty-second trail suppression can cover an entire rotation."],"cons":["Aura trigger is one-time per generator.","Stealth half can be wasted by poor timing.","No direct action-speed bonus."],"analysis":["Poised deserves this position because its modern version quietly bundles two useful effects into ordinary generator play. Touching a fresh generator grants an eight-second Killer Aura read, which is enough time to decide whether the objective is safe before committing.","The second half triggers on any generator completion, not only one you finish. Thirty seconds without Scratch Marks can support a long rotation or a chase transition if the timing lines up with Killer pressure.","The perk is particularly good in Solo Q because it supplies information without requiring teammate coordination. You are rewarded for doing the main objective, and the information can prevent a bad repair commitment before the Killer arrives.","Poised stays in B because neither effect is under perfect player control. A generator can finish while you are nowhere near danger, and Aura denial can blunt the first-repair read. Still, the 9.2 buffs made it a much more complete perk than older rankings suggest."],"verdict":"A strong passive objective-information hybrid. Poised now gives enough Killer vision and post-gen stealth to justify a real build slot, especially in Solo Q.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Jane Romero"},"synergyPerkIds":["deja-vu","lightweight","fixated","quick-quiet"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"synergies":["Déjà Vu","Lightweight","Fixated","Quick & Quiet"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Poised","alternateName":null,"source":"Jane Romero","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever a Generator is completed, suppresses your Scratch Marks for 20/25/30 seconds. The first time you start repairing each Generator, reveals the Killer's Aura to you for 8 seconds.","activation":["A Generator is completed for the Scratch Mark effect.","Start repairing a given Generator for the first time for its Killer-aura reveal.","Ends/deactivates when: Scratch Mark suppression ends after 20/25/30 seconds.","Ends/deactivates when: The Killer Aura reveal ends after 8 seconds and does not trigger again for that Generator."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.2.0): Increased Scratch Mark suppression to 20/25/30 seconds and Killer Aura reveal on first repair of each Generator to 8 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"Generator completions hide your Scratch Marks temporarily, and starting each Generator for the first time reveals the Killer briefly.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Scratch Mark suppression: 20/25/30 seconds after each Generator completion.","Killer Aura reveal: 8 seconds on the first repair start for each Generator."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"The Killer Aura component triggers only on the first repair start of each individual Generator.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Jane Romero","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"blast-mine","rank":49,"tier":"B","roles":["Objective","Chase","Information"],"summary":"After 40% generator repair, trap a Generator for up to 120 seconds; if the Killer kicks it, they are stunned for 4 seconds and nearby players are blinded.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["pressure","aura-reading"],"useCases":["Punish a Killer who repeatedly returns to kick a contested generator.","Use the yellow Generator Aura to communicate an important objective to teammates.","Buy four seconds of Killer downtime during a regression attempt."],"counters":["The Killer must actually damage the trapped generator.","A trap can expire unused.","The blind can affect nearby Survivors too."],"pros":["Four-second Killer stun is meaningful time.","Easy to charge through normal repair.","Trap also marks the generator for the team."],"cons":["Trigger is Killer-controlled.","Does not stop the initial decision to pressure the generator.","Can become mostly entertainment value if the stunned Killer was not losing meaningful tempo."],"analysis":["Blast Mine ranks this position because a four-second stun is real Killer downtime attached to normal generator participation. Forty percent total repair is a reasonable charge condition, so many Trials offer multiple opportunities to arm it.","The yellow Aura also gives the perk a communication layer. Teammates can identify the trapped generator and infer that it is strategically important, which matters more in Solo Q than the text first suggests.","The weakness is agency. The Killer can ignore the generator, let the mine expire, or arrive only after the situation no longer matters. Unlike a chase stun, the Survivor cannot force the trigger.","That puts Blast Mine in a useful but conditional band. It is easy, useful, and occasionally disruptive, but too dependent on Killer behavior to outrank more reliable information and support tools."],"verdict":"A satisfying and legitimately useful regression punish. Blast Mine buys real time when it triggers, but the Killer decides whether the trigger ever happens.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Stun"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Jill Valentine"},"synergyPerkIds":["wiretap","deja-vu","residual-manifest","champion-of-light"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Wiretap","Déjà Vu","Residual Manifest","Champion of Light"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Blast Mine","alternateName":null,"source":"Jill Valentine","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After you repair Generators for a total of 40%, install a trap on a Generator with the Active Ability button. If the Killer begins damaging it, the trap triggers halfway through the action, stuns the Killer for 4 seconds and blinds players within 12.5 metres. All Survivors see its yellow Aura. The trap expires after 100/110/120 seconds if unused.","activation":["Accumulate 40% total Generator repair progress.","Install the trap on a Generator.","Ends/deactivates when: Trap is consumed when triggered or expires after its tier duration."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.2.0): Changed the activation requirement to 40% total Generator repair progress.","plainEnglishSummary":"After enough Generator repair, you can booby-trap a Generator to stun the Killer who damages it.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Trap duration: 100/110/120 seconds.","Killer stun: 4 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"One trap per activation; another requires reactivation.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Triggers halfway through the Killer's Generator damage action.","Blinds players within 12.5 metres; all Survivors see its yellow Aura."],"sourceCharacter":"Jill Valentine","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"windows-of-opportunity","rank":50,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Information"],"summary":"See nearby Window Auras and vault Windows 10% faster, with a cooldown after each Window vault.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","looping","pre-drop","greed","solo-q"],"useCases":["Identify nearby Windows quickly in unfamiliar structures.","Turn close Window timings into safer escapes with 10% faster vaults.","Use the Aura layer to plan a Window-heavy chase route before committing."],"counters":["Vaulting a Window puts the entire perk on cooldown for 40/35/30 seconds.","It no longer reveals Pallets or Breakable Walls.","Twenty-four metres is much less map coverage than the old Tier III range."],"pros":["10% faster Window vaulting is direct chase power.","Window Auras still help unfamiliar-map routing.","Works at every health state."],"cons":["Lost Pallet and Breakable Wall information in 10.2.","Cooldown means the Aura and speed package is not permanent.","Much less beginner macro coverage than the pre-10.2 version."],"analysis":["Windows of Opportunity changed identity in 10.2. It is no longer the always-on all-resource map overlay that justified an elite information ranking; it now specializes in Windows and directly accelerates vaults by 10%.","The faster vault is meaningful. Tight Window timings decide many hits, and a ten-percent modifier can turn a marginal connection into a clean escape. The nearby Window Auras also remain useful when a structure is unfamiliar or visually cluttered.","The cost is information breadth and uptime. Pallets and Breakable Walls disappeared from the perk, the Aura range is fixed at 24 metres, and every Window vault starts a 40/35/30-second cooldown.","That makes modern Windows more of a chase-tech perk than a universal teaching tool. It can still be strong, but the old top-ten logic based on permanent Pallet-and-Window knowledge no longer applies and must be re-audited."],"verdict":"Still a legitimate chase perk, but no longer the universal resource radar it used to be. The 10% vault bonus keeps it relevant while the cooldown and loss of Pallet information demand a lower fresh ranking.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:audit-explicit"],"tags":["Vault"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[42,60],"rankConfidence":"Medium","rankStatus":"provisional","evidenceStatus":"provisional-direction-stable","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Kate Denson"},"synergyPerkIds":["finesse","lithe","resilience","quick-quiet"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Finesse","Lithe","Resilience","Quick & Quiet"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Windows of Opportunity","alternateName":null,"source":"Kate Denson","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Within 24 metres, you see the Auras of Windows. You vault Windows 10% faster. Whenever you vault a Window, the perk goes on cooldown for 40/35/30 seconds.","activation":["A Window is within 24 metres for its Aura to be revealed.","Vault a Window to receive the 10% faster Window-vault effect while the perk is available.","Ends/deactivates when: After vaulting a Window, the perk is on cooldown for 40/35/30 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Complete rework: now reveals only Window Auras within 24 metres, grants 10% faster Window vaults, and enters a 40/35/30-second cooldown after vaulting a Window.","plainEnglishSummary":"See nearby Windows and vault them faster, with a tiered cooldown after each Window vault.","cooldown":"40/35/30 seconds after vaulting a Window.","duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The 10.2.0 rework removes Pallet and Breakable Wall Aura reading; only Windows are revealed."],"sourceCharacter":"Kate Denson","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"smash-hit","rank":51,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Exhaustion","Pallet"],"summary":"After you Pallet-stun the Killer, gain 50% Haste for 4 seconds and only 20 seconds of Exhaustion at Tier III.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["haste","exhausted","looping"],"useCases":["Turn a successful pallet stun into enough distance to leave the tile entirely.","Exploit the short Exhaustion timer for repeat use in long matches.","Pair with stun-oriented builds that already aim to land pallets."],"counters":["Requires an actual pallet stun, not merely a drop.","Cannot activate while already Exhausted.","Strong Killers can respect pallets and avoid giving clean stun opportunities.","Hex: Under Your Thumb can cap running Haste while the Hex remains lit."],"pros":["Four seconds at 50% Haste is a huge burst.","Very short Exhaustion compared with classic perks.","Excellent reward for a successful chase interaction."],"cons":["Trigger is much less reliable than a vault or start-running condition.","Requires pallet resources.","Can be dead against Killers or players who rarely take pallet stuns."],"analysis":["Smash Hit takes this position because four seconds of 50% Haste is one of the largest Exhaustion payoffs in the game. A landed pallet stun can immediately become enough distance to abandon the tile and reach a much stronger resource.","The 20-second Tier III Exhaustion timer is another major strength. If the match contains enough chase downtime, Smash Hit can realistically return before another important chase much sooner than Sprint Burst or Lithe.","The reason it remains B is simple: the activation is not guaranteed. Good Killers often respect pallets, use powers through them, or force early drops that never stun. The perk is only as reliable as the user's ability to create the correct pallet interaction.","Players who are already strong at pallet timing can extract much more value than average users. It is a high-ceiling chase perk, but not a universal one."],"verdict":"A huge reward for a condition the Killer can often deny. Smash Hit is excellent in practiced pallet hands, but too trigger-dependent for the top chase tier.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Lee Yun-Jin"},"synergyPerkIds":["five-moves-ahead","parental-guidance","any-means-necessary"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Five Moves Ahead","Parental Guidance","Any Means Necessary"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Smash Hit","alternateName":null,"source":"Lee Yun-Jin","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After you stun the Killer with a Pallet, gain 50% Haste for 4 seconds. You cannot use Smash Hit while Exhausted; using it applies Exhausted for 30/25/20 seconds.","activation":["Stun the Killer with a Pallet.","You must not be Exhausted.","Ends/deactivates when: Haste ends after 4 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (7.1.0): Reduced the Exhausted duration to 30/25/20 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"A successful Pallet stun gives you a short speed burst and then Exhausted.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Haste: 4 seconds.","Exhausted: 30/25/20 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Haste","Exhausted"],"specialInteractions":["Shares the Exhausted status-effect recovery rules with other Exhaustion perks."],"sourceCharacter":"Lee Yun-Jin","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"chemical-trap","rank":52,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Pallet"],"summary":"After enough generator repair, trap a dropped Pallet so breaking it inflicts a severe 50% Hindered effect on the Killer for 4 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["looping","pressure"],"useCases":["Trap a strong dropped pallet that the Killer is likely to break before the 60-second timer expires.","Create enough post-break distance to reach another tile after the Killer commits to the pallet.","Signal the trapped pallet to teammates through its yellow Aura."],"counters":["Requires 20% total generator repair before activation.","The trap expires if the Killer does not break the pallet during its timer.","The Killer can sometimes play around the pallet or leave it intact."],"pros":["50% Hindered for 4 seconds is a very large chase swing.","Relatively low repair requirement to charge.","All Survivors can see the trapped pallet."],"cons":["Needs a dropped pallet and a Killer willing to break it.","One trap may expire without ever triggering.","Does not help at tiles where the Killer can safely ignore the pallet."],"analysis":["Chemical Trap is valuable here because its payoff is excellent but opportunity-dependent. A 50% Hindered effect for four seconds after a pallet break creates enormous separation and can turn a normally short post-break transition into a clean escape to another structure.","The repair requirement is no longer oppressive. Twenty percent total generator contribution is easy to earn during normal objective play, so the real question is whether the Survivor can place the trap on a pallet the Killer actually needs to break before the timer expires.","Strong placement is a skill. A weak pallet the Killer can ignore is a poor trap target, while a major resource that blocks the Killer's path is much more reliable. Any Means Necessary adds interesting synergy because the player already has pallet-state information and can interact with abandoned pallets.","The perk ranks below more reliable general-purpose perks because the Killer retains agency over the trigger. A trap that expires produces no chase value at all. When it detonates at the right tile, however, the slowdown is strong enough to justify a dedicated chase slot."],"verdict":"A potent chase trap with an unreliable trigger. Chemical Trap's 50% Hindered effect is excellent, but only if you place it where the Killer truly has to break the pallet.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Hindered"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Ellen Ripley"},"synergyPerkIds":["any-means-necessary","champion-of-light","lithe"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Any Means Necessary","Champion of Light","Lithe"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Chemical Trap","alternateName":null,"source":"Ellen Ripley","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After repairing Generators for a total of 20%, install a Trap on a dropped Pallet with the Active Ability button. It lasts 40/50/60 seconds. When the Killer breaks the trapped Pallet, they suffer 50% Hindered for 4 seconds and the Trap is consumed. All Survivors see the Pallet's yellow Aura.","activation":["Accumulate 20% total Generator repair progress.","Install the trap on a dropped Pallet.","Ends/deactivates when: Trap is consumed when triggered or expires after its tier duration."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.2.0): Reduced the activation threshold to 20% total Generator repair progress and the trap duration to 40/50/60 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"After enough Generator repair, trap a dropped Pallet to slow the Killer if they break it.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Trap duration: 40/50/60 seconds.","Killer Hindered: 4 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"One trap per activation; another requires qualifying progress and installation.","statusEffectsInvolved":["Hindered"],"specialInteractions":["All Survivors see the trapped Pallet's Aura in yellow."],"sourceCharacter":"Ellen Ripley","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"dance-with-me","rank":53,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Stealth"],"summary":"After a fast or medium vault or fast Locker exit, leave no Scratch Marks for 5 seconds; cooldown is only 15 seconds at Tier III.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["looping"],"useCases":["Break line of sight at a vault and immediately hide the route you took afterward.","Pair with Lithe or Quick & Quiet to convert vault distance into a complete tracking break.","Use frequent 15-second cycles during longer chases."],"counters":["The Killer can still hear you, see Blood, read Auras, or maintain direct sight.","Five seconds is short if you do not immediately exploit a route split.","Open tiles provide fewer opportunities to create ambiguity."],"pros":["Short cooldown.","Easy trigger through common chase actions.","Excellent synergy with Lithe."],"cons":["Only hides Scratch Marks.","Brief duration.","Requires good pathing after the vault to create real confusion."],"analysis":["Dance With Me ranks this position because the modern 15-second cooldown gives it enough frequency to become a real chase tool rather than an occasional stealth trick. Vaulting is already central to Survivor pathing, so the trigger is natural.","The best pairing remains Lithe. The speed burst creates distance while Dance With Me erases the trail, forcing the Killer to reacquire the Survivor through sight or sound instead of following a clean route.","The perk's weakness is coverage. Scratch Marks are only one tracking channel, and five seconds disappears quickly. A Survivor who vaults and then runs down an obvious corridor gains little.","That makes Dance With Me skill-sensitive chase utility. It is strong when the route after the vault contains real choices and merely decorative when it does not."],"verdict":"A good chase-stealth perk with excellent Lithe synergy. Dance With Me rewards immediate route changes after a vault, not simply the absence of red marks.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Tracking Denial"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Kate Denson"},"synergyPerkIds":["lithe","quick-quiet","lightweight","lucky-break"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Lithe","Quick & Quiet","Lightweight","Lucky Break"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Dance With Me","alternateName":null,"source":"Kate Denson","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Performing a Rushed action to vault a Window or exit a Locker suppresses your Scratch Marks for 5 seconds. Cooldown: 25/20/15 seconds by tier.","activation":["Perform a Rushed Window vault or exit a Locker with a Rushed action.","Ends/deactivates when: Scratch Mark suppression ends after 5 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.6.0): Increased Scratch Mark suppression from 3 to 5 seconds and reduced cooldown from 30/25/20 to 25/20/15 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"A rushed Window vault or Locker exit hides your Scratch Marks briefly.","cooldown":"25/20/15 seconds by tier","duration":["Scratch Marks suppressed for 5 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Kate Denson","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"flow-state","rank":54,"tier":"B","roles":["Team Support","Healing"],"summary":"Each completed Generator permanently adds a Token that massively speeds your healing, unhooking, cleansing, and blessing actions, up to five Tokens.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["reset","hook-state"],"useCases":["Scale into faster heals and unhooks as the Trial progresses.","Improve Totem interaction speed in Boon or anti-Hex builds.","Use late-game Tokens to make rescue and reset interactions noticeably faster."],"counters":["The perk starts with zero Tokens.","Early-game value is limited until generators are completed.","It does not accelerate generator repair itself."],"pros":["Multiple useful action categories scale from the same Tokens.","Requires no active management after generators are completed.","Late-game bonuses can become large if the team has progressed well."],"cons":["Win-more tendency because the perk strengthens as generators are completed.","No effect on the objective that generates its Tokens.","Weakest during the early game when establishing momentum matters most."],"analysis":["Flow State received one of the largest numerical buffs in 10.2. Each Generator Token now adds 13/14/15% action speed to healing, unhooking, blessing, and cleansing, still stacking up to five times.","The scaling becomes meaningful much earlier than endgame. At Tier III, two completed generators already represent 30% faster support actions, while three represent 45%. Those are numbers that can materially change rescue and reset timing.","The structural weakness remains that the perk starts at zero. It cannot prevent an early snowball before generators are completed, and it does not accelerate generator repair itself.","Even with that caveat, the old lower-B evaluation is too conservative after the buff. Flow State should be one of the first perks an independent reviewer reconsiders upward."],"verdict":"A much stronger scaling support perk in 10.2. It still starts asleep, but every completed Generator now wakes it up far more aggressively.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"tags":["Support","Scaling"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Kwon Tae-Young"},"synergyPerkIds":["boon-circle-of-healing","boon-steadfast","well-make-it","lend-a-hand"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Boon: Circle of Healing","Boon: Steadfast","We'll Make It","Lend a Hand"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Flow State","alternateName":null,"source":"Kwon Tae-Young","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever a Generator is completed, gain 1 Token, up to 5. For each Token, you Bless and Cleanse Totems, heal, and unhook Survivors 13/14/15% faster.","activation":["A Generator must be completed to gain a Token."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Increased each per-Token Bless/Cleanse, healing, and unhook speed bonus from 8/9/10% to 13/14/15%.","plainEnglishSummary":"Generator completions build permanent tokens that increasingly speed Totem interactions, healing, and unhooking.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Tokens and their action-speed bonuses persist for the remainder of the Trial; no expiry is stated."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Gain 1 Token whenever any Generator is completed, up to 5. Tokens are not spent; each one adds the tier's action-speed bonus to blessing/cleansing, healing, and unhooking.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Maximum of 5 Tokens.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Kwon Tae-Young","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"troubleshooter","rank":55,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Information","Objective"],"summary":"While chased, see the most-progressed Generator; after dropping a Pallet, see the Killer for up to 6 seconds, with both effects lingering briefly after chase.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","pressure","looping","solo-q"],"useCases":["Avoid dragging the Killer onto the team's most important generator.","Read the Killer through walls after pallet drops to win mindgames.","Use the linger after chase to reposition around the most-progressed objective."],"counters":["Requires being in chase for the generator Aura effect.","Pallet Aura read only happens after you drop a pallet.","Strong direct-vision Killers may reduce the need for the information."],"pros":["Excellent beginner and Solo Q chase information.","Protects team macro while helping tile-level mindgames.","No cooldown or token management."],"cons":["No direct speed or health-state protection.","Requires active chase.","Information only matters if the user can act on it."],"analysis":["Troubleshooter remains one of the cleaner mid-tier information perks because both halves solve real Survivor mistakes. The most-progressed Generator Aura tells the chased player exactly where not to route the Killer.","After a pallet drop, the Killer Aura read removes much of the guesswork from the next few seconds of the loop. That is particularly helpful at tall or visually cluttered structures where standard mindgames depend on losing sight.","The perk is very friendly to developing players because it teaches both chase and macro habits. Experienced players still get value, but often know the same information through game sense or communication.","It stays in B because it never creates raw distance. The perk improves decisions rather than changing the physics of the chase."],"verdict":"A superb learning and Solo Q information perk. Troubleshooter makes both chase routing and pallet mindgames cleaner, but remains an information tool rather than direct protection.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Gabriel Soma"},"synergyPerkIds":["five-moves-ahead","resilience","quick-gambit"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"synergies":["Five Moves Ahead","Resilience","Quick Gambit"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Troubleshooter","alternateName":null,"source":"Gabriel Soma","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While chased by the Killer, reveals the Aura of the Generator with the most progress. After you drop a Pallet, reveals the Killer's Aura for 4/5/6 seconds. The effects linger for 6/8/10 seconds after the Chase ends, then the perk deactivates.","activation":["Be chased by the Killer to reveal the most-progressed Generator.","Drop a Pallet during the effect to reveal the Killer's Aura.","Ends/deactivates when: Effects linger for 6/8/10 seconds after the Chase ends, then deactivate."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified from available patch history.","plainEnglishSummary":"During and briefly after a chase, shows the most-progressed Generator and can reveal the Killer after you drop a Pallet.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Killer Aura reveal after dropping a Pallet: 4/5/6 seconds.","Perk linger after Chase ends: 6/8/10 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The Generator Aura shown is the one with the most progress at activation."],"sourceCharacter":"Gabriel Soma","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"do-no-harm","rank":56,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Team Support"],"summary":"Heal teammates faster for each Hook State they have, reaching up to 80% faster at two Hook States, with stronger and more frequent Great healing Skill Checks.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["hook-state","reset","health-state"],"useCases":["Reset a death-hook teammate extremely quickly.","Combine with healing builds to make late-game support very efficient.","Exploit Great Skill Checks for additional progress on already-hooked teammates."],"counters":["Provides no bonus on teammates with zero Hook States.","Requires direct teammate healing.","The strongest bonus appears only on Survivors already close to elimination."],"pros":["Very large healing ceiling on death-hook teammates.","Targets the teammates who most need safe resets.","Strong SWF triage value."],"cons":["Conditional on Hook States.","No self-heal benefit.","Can be redundant if another perk already makes the heal nearly instant."],"analysis":["Do No Harm remains a strong triage perk, but its 10.2 Tier III ceiling is now 40% faster healing per Hook State, or 80% on a teammate with two Hook States.","The Skill Check package adds more texture: Great basic healing checks grant 3% extra progress and Hook States also increase the chance that healing Skill Checks occur.","That makes the perk especially effective on the teammate the team most needs to protect, because death-hook Survivors receive both the largest speed bonus and more opportunities for bonus progress.","It is still conditional on the target having Hook States, so the opening of a Trial can remain quiet. The 10.2 adjustments reduce the raw ceiling slightly while making the Skill Check portion more reliable."],"verdict":"Still a strong death-hook triage perk. The live ceiling is now 80% faster healing at two Hook States, with more Skill Check opportunities supporting the reset.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:audit-explicit"],"tags":["Support","Scaling"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[50,66],"rankConfidence":"Low","rankStatus":"provisional","evidenceStatus":"needs-controlled-testing","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Orela Rose"},"synergyPerkIds":["botany-knowledge","well-make-it","desperate-measures","empathy"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Botany Knowledge","We'll Make It","Desperate Measures","Empathy"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Do No Harm","alternateName":null,"source":"Orela Rose","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While healing another Survivor, for each Hook State they have: you heal 30/35/40% faster, Great basic Skill Checks grant 3% more progress, and the odds of triggering a Skill Check increase by 5%.","activation":["Heal another Survivor; all three bonuses scale with that Survivor's Hook States and do nothing at zero Hook States.","Ends/deactivates when: The bonuses apply only while healing another Survivor."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Adjusted healing speed to 30/35/40% per Hook State, tied the +3% Great basic Skill Check progress to Hook States, and added +5% Skill Check occurrence chance.","plainEnglishSummary":"Healing a teammate who has Hook States is faster, gives stronger Great basic Skill Check progress, and causes Skill Checks more often, all scaling with each Hook State.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Great basic Healing Skill Checks grant +3% progress per Hook State of the Survivor being healed.","Healing Skill Check occurrence chance is increased by 5% per Hook State of the Survivor being healed (maximum 10% at 2 Hook States)."],"sourceCharacter":"Orela Rose","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"extrasensory-perception","rank":57,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Stealth"],"summary":"After crouching for 4 seconds, reveal Survivors, the Killer, and many map objects in an expanding radius up to 44 metres while gaining Elusive and Oblivious.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading"],"useCases":["Scout a dangerous area before committing to an objective or rescue.","Use Elusive during the scan to avoid Aura reads and trail tracking.","Identify nearby pallets, windows, totems, chests, objectives, and players at once."],"counters":["Requires four seconds of crouching setup.","Oblivious removes Terror Radius information during the effect.","Forty-second Tier III cooldown limits repeated scans."],"pros":["Extremely broad information payload.","Elusive protects several tracking channels during use.","Can solve unfamiliar indoor maps quickly."],"cons":["Setup time is substantial.","Oblivious can create risk if used carelessly.","Information overload may not translate into actual tempo."],"analysis":["Extrasensory Perception ranks this position because few perks show so much information at once. A completed scan can reveal players, the Killer, generators, pallets, windows, Totems, chests, gates, items, and more within the growing radius.","The built-in Elusive state is important because the user is otherwise vulnerable while crouching. Aura, Scratch-Mark, Blood, and pain-sound suppression make the scouting moment safer against information-heavy Killers.","The price is tempo and awareness. Four seconds of crouching is not free, and Oblivious means the Terror Radius disappears while the scan is active. A badly timed activation can make the user less aware of a Killer approaching from outside the revealed area.","That mixture of huge information and meaningful setup keeps it in B. Strong players can use it as a deliberate scouting tool, while casual use risks turning it into expensive sightseeing."],"verdict":"A broad, powerful scouting perk with a real setup tax. Extrasensory Perception can answer almost every local information question at once, but only if you choose a safe moment to ask.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Scouting"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Eleven"},"synergyPerkIds":["urban-evasion","open-handed","inner-strength","boon-shadow-step"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Urban Evasion","Open-Handed","Inner Strength","Boon: Shadow Step"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Extrasensory Perception","alternateName":null,"source":"Eleven","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Crouch for 4 seconds to activate. While active, you see Auras of Survivors, the Killer, and Chests, Exit Gates, Generators, the Hatch, Items, Pallets, Totems, and Windows in an expanding radius up to 44 metres. You gain Elusive and Oblivious. The effect ends when you stop crouching or after 11 seconds, then the perk goes on a 60/50/40-second cooldown.","activation":["Crouch for 4 seconds.","Ends/deactivates when: All effects end when you stop crouching.","Ends/deactivates when: All effects end after 11 seconds even if you remain crouched."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.4.0): Introduced; no later material live balance change located in the official notes checked.","plainEnglishSummary":"After crouching to focus, you briefly reveal nearby people and objects while becoming Elusive and Oblivious.","cooldown":"60/50/40 seconds (Tier I/II/III), beginning when the effect ends.","duration":["Activation requires 4 seconds of crouching.","Maximum active duration: 11 seconds.","Aura radius expands up to 44 metres while active."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Elusive","Oblivious"],"specialInteractions":["The listed Aura reveals include Survivors, the Killer, Chests, Exit Gates, Generators, the Hatch, Items, Pallets, Totems, and Windows."],"sourceCharacter":"Eleven","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"salvations-cry","rank":58,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Information"],"summary":"When the Killer starts chasing you, briefly show teammates to you and show both you and the Killer to every teammate not in chase.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","pressure","solo-q","swf"],"useCases":["Give the entire team immediate Killer information when your chase begins.","Help teammates know whether the chase is moving toward their generator or rescue path.","Use the brief teammate Auras to route away from active objectives."],"counters":["Only triggers when a chase officially begins.","The user sees teammates for only up to 3 seconds.","Teammates already in chase do not receive the same team-information package."],"pros":["Teamwide information from a natural chase event.","No cooldown or setup stated in the current effect.","Particularly useful for SWF-like coordination in Solo Q."],"cons":["Short personal Aura duration.","No direct chase power.","Official chase detection can occasionally behave differently from player intuition."],"analysis":["Salvation's Cry lands at this position because it broadcasts one of the most important match facts, the start of a chase, to the rest of the team. Survivors not being chased see both the chased Survivor and the Killer for five seconds.","That information immediately answers macro questions. A teammate can stay on a generator if the Killer is moving away, rotate early if the chase is coming toward them, or abandon a risky rescue path before the Killer arrives.","The chased player also gets a short teammate Aura snapshot, helping them avoid dragging the Killer onto active objectives. That overlaps conceptually with Quick Gambit, though without the repair-speed bonus.","It remains B because the perk changes information rather than chase physics. The team must convert the five-second read into better decisions for the slot to matter."],"verdict":"A clean team-information perk that makes chase starts visible to everyone. Salvation's Cry is especially valuable when Solo Q needs SWF-like awareness without voice comms.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Team Information","Aura Reading"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Aurora Stardotter"},"synergyPerkIds":["quick-gambit","kindred","bond","poised"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"synergies":["Quick Gambit","Kindred","Bond","Poised"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Salvation's Cry","alternateName":null,"source":"Aurora Stardotter","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever the Killer starts chasing you, you see the Auras of all other Survivors for 1/2/3 seconds. Every Survivor who is not being chased sees your Aura and the Killer's Aura for 5 seconds.","activation":["The Killer must start chasing you.","Ends/deactivates when: Aura reveals end after their stated durations."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.1.0): Added as a new Aurora Stardotter perk; no later live balance change verified.","plainEnglishSummary":"When a chase starts on you, briefly shares Survivor and Killer locations with everyone not in chase.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Other Survivors' Auras are visible to you for 1/2/3 seconds.","Your Aura and the Killer's Aura are visible to each Survivor not being chased for 5 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The shared Aura reveal is limited to Survivors who are not currently being chased."],"sourceCharacter":"Aurora Stardotter","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"borrowed-time","rank":59,"tier":"B","roles":["Anti-Tunnel","Rescue"],"summary":"Extend a rescued Survivor's base unhook Endurance by up to 10 seconds and their Haste by another 10 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["endurance","anti-tunnel","hook-state","conspicuous-action"],"useCases":["Protect a rescue when the Killer remains near the hook.","Give the unhooked Survivor more time to reach a safe tile before protections expire.","Stack longer Endurance with coordinated bodyblocks or endgame saves."],"counters":["Only affects Survivors you unhook.","Conspicuous Actions still end Endurance early.","The modern base game already grants meaningful unhook protection without the perk.","Hex: Under Your Thumb can cap running Haste while the Hex remains lit."],"pros":["Simple anti-tunnel extension.","No cooldown or token system.","Excellent for dangerous endgame rescues."],"cons":["Partially overlaps basekit unhook protection.","No Killer information.","Does not help if the Killer ignores the rescued Survivor."],"analysis":["Borrowed Time sits at this position because it is still good, but the base game absorbed much of what once made it mandatory. Every unhook already provides Endurance and Haste, so the perk now extends protection rather than creating it.","That extension is still meaningful. Twenty total seconds of Endurance at Tier III can force a camping Killer to wait much longer or commit into protection that would otherwise have expired.","The perk is particularly valuable in endgame or forced-trade scenarios, where there may be no safer macro option than rescuing under direct pressure. SWF can coordinate around the extended timer very effectively.","It ranks below Babysitter because Babysitter provides speed, trail denial, and Killer information in one slot. Borrowed Time remains dependable, but narrower."],"verdict":"Still a respectable rescue perk, no longer a mandatory one. Borrowed Time is best when you expect the Killer to pressure the unhooked Survivor for longer than basekit protection covers.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"tags":["Endurance"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"William \"Bill\" Overbeck"},"synergyPerkIds":["babysitter","shoulder-the-burden","kindred","well-make-it"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Babysitter","Shoulder the Burden","Kindred","We'll Make It"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Borrowed Time","alternateName":null,"source":"William \"Bill\" Overbeck","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"When you unhook another Survivor, extend their Endurance by 6/8/10 seconds to 16/18/20 seconds total and extend their Haste by 10 seconds to 20 seconds total. Endurance is cancelled early if they perform a Conspicuous Action.","activation":["Unhook another Survivor.","Ends/deactivates when: Endurance ends early if rescued Survivor performs a Conspicuous Action.","Ends/deactivates when: Both effects expire after their durations."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (6.1.0): Reworked the perk to extend Endurance by 6/8/10 seconds and movement-speed bonus by 10 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"Unhooking a teammate extends their post-unhook Endurance and Haste protections.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Endurance total: 16/18/20 seconds by tier.","Haste total: 20 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Endurance","Haste"],"specialInteractions":["Extends post-unhook protections."],"sourceCharacter":"William \"Bill\" Overbeck","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"we-see-you","rank":60,"tier":"B","roles":["Information"],"summary":"Each time the Killer reveals your Aura, gain a Token; at 4 Tokens, reveal the Killer to the entire team for up to 15 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","swf"],"useCases":["Punish Aura-heavy Killer builds with a long teamwide reveal.","Pair with Bound by Obsession to intentionally generate Aura interactions.","Use the 15-second Killer read to coordinate objectives, rescues, and chase routing."],"counters":["Needs four Killer Aura reveals before paying out.","A ten-second cooldown limits token gain speed.","Aura-light Killers may never activate the payoff."],"pros":["Fifteen seconds of teamwide Killer Aura is extremely strong.","Automatically reacts to Killer information perks.","Strong SWF planning tool once triggered."],"cons":["Very matchup dependent.","Slow setup against occasional Aura reads.","Can be completely dead against certain builds."],"analysis":["We See You takes this position because its payoff is far stronger than its setup reliability. Four Killer Aura reads are converted into a teamwide Killer Aura reveal lasting up to fifteen seconds, which is a huge information window.","Against Aura-heavy Killers, tokens can arrive naturally throughout the Trial. The perk becomes even more deliberate when paired with Bound by Obsession, which creates predictable Aura interactions while giving the user reciprocal information.","The problem is the floor. A Killer with little Aura reading may never feed four tokens, leaving the perk without its defining effect. That kind of matchup dependence prevents a higher placement.","When it triggers, however, the entire team can make informed decisions for a long stretch of the match. We See You is therefore a high-ceiling but conditional information perk."],"verdict":"A powerful anti-Aura payoff trapped behind a matchup check. If the Killer repeatedly reads you, We See You can repay the favor with fifteen seconds of teamwide vision.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Aura Reading","Team Information","Counter-Intel"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Eleven"},"synergyPerkIds":["bound-by-obsession","distortion","open-handed","kindred"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"synergies":["Bound by Obsession","Distortion","Open-Handed","Kindred"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"We See You","alternateName":null,"source":"Eleven","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Gain 1 Token when the Killer reveals your Aura. When you reach 4 Tokens, consume all 4 and reveal the Killer's Aura to you and all other Survivors for 10/12.5/15 seconds. There is a 10-second cooldown between token gains.","activation":["The Killer must reveal your Aura to earn tokens.","Four tokens are required to trigger the shared Killer Aura reveal.","Ends/deactivates when: The Killer Aura reveal ends after 10/12.5/15 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.4.0): Introduced; no later material live balance change located in the official notes checked.","plainEnglishSummary":"When the Killer reveals your Aura, you build tokens toward a team-wide Killer Aura reveal.","cooldown":"10 seconds between token gains","duration":["Shared Killer Aura reveal: 10/12.5/15 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Gain 1 token each time the Killer reveals your Aura, no more often than once per 10 seconds. At 4 tokens, all tokens are consumed to reveal the Killer's Aura to all Survivors.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The Aura reveal is shared with all Survivors, not just the perk user."],"sourceCharacter":"Eleven","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"champion-of-light","rank":61,"tier":"B","roles":["Item","Chase"],"summary":"Move faster while shining a Flashlight, and after any blind inflict 20% Hindered on the Killer for 6 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["haste","looping"],"useCases":["Use Flashlight movement speed to reposition around blind attempts and pallet interactions.","Convert a successful Killer blind into a six-second Hindered window that creates extra chase distance.","Pair with save-oriented Flashlight play so successful blinds also improve the escape afterward."],"counters":["Requires a Flashlight for the primary movement effect and reliable access to blinds for the secondary effect.","Blind-resistant play, facing walls, or Lightborn can deny much of the build plan.","The Hindered effect has a cooldown after a successful blind."],"pros":["Successful blinds gain a meaningful chase payoff beyond visual denial.","Works with blinds from multiple sources for the Hindered component.","Cooldown was reduced in 9.0.0."],"cons":["Highly equipment- and execution-dependent.","Can produce no value in a match where blinds are consistently denied.","Encourages a specialized playstyle rather than broad team utility."],"analysis":["Champion of Light ranks this position because the secondary effect is genuinely powerful: after a blind, the Killer suffers 20% Hindered for six seconds. That can convert a normal blind into much more distance, especially at a pallet or during a rescue where the Survivor needs to escape immediately afterward.","The problem is access. The movement-speed portion requires actively shining a Flashlight, and the meaningful slowdown requires a successful blind. Killers can face walls during pickups, look away during transitions, or equip Lightborn, all of which reduce the number of opportunities the perk receives.","Skilled Flashlight users get much more value than average players. They already understand blind timings and angles, so Champion of Light simply adds another reward to actions they were going to attempt anyway. Background Player and Flashbang also create specialized builds where multiple blind tools support the same strategy.","That specialization is why we place it in B rather than A despite a strong numerical effect. A perk that requires both the correct equipment and repeated execution should not outrank broad information, healing, or chase tools that function in nearly every match."],"verdict":"A strong specialist perk for confident blind players. Champion of Light makes successful blinds much more punishing, but its floor is too equipment-dependent to be a universal recommendation.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Flashlight","Hindered"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Alan Wake"},"synergyPerkIds":["flashbang","background-player","chemical-trap","residual-manifest"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Flashbang","Background Player","Chemical Trap","Residual Manifest"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Champion of Light","alternateName":null,"source":"Alan Wake","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While shining a Flashlight, gain 50% Haste. After blinding the Killer by any means, they suffer 20% Hindered for 6 seconds. The perk then has a 60/50/40-second cooldown.","activation":["Shine a Flashlight for Haste.","Blind the Killer by any means to apply Hindered.","Ends/deactivates when: Haste applies while shining the Flashlight.","Ends/deactivates when: Hindered ends after 6 seconds; perk cooldown follows."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.0.0): Reduced the cooldown to 60/50/40 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"Shining a Flashlight speeds you up, and blinding the Killer briefly Hinders them.","cooldown":"60/50/40 seconds by tier","duration":["Killer Hindered: 6 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Haste","Hindered"],"specialInteractions":["The blind may be caused by any means; after its Hindered effect, this perk has a cooldown."],"sourceCharacter":"Alan Wake","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"quick-gambit","rank":62,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Objective","Team Support"],"summary":"While you are being chased, see teammate Auras and make every other Survivor repair up to 5% faster; losing a Health State starts a 40-second cooldown.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["pressure","aura-reading","swf","solo-q","looping"],"useCases":["Turn a long chase into extra generator progress for the entire team.","Use teammate Auras to avoid dragging the Killer onto active generators.","Coordinate chase routes in SWF so repair-heavy teammates stay uninterrupted."],"counters":["Taking damage starts the cooldown.","If teammates are healing or rescuing instead of repairing, the repair bonus does nothing.","Short chases produce little total objective value."],"pros":["Rewards exactly the team behavior Survivors already want during a good chase.","Can affect multiple teammates at once.","Aura information helps the chased player protect teammates' positions."],"cons":["Value depends on surviving chase for meaningful time.","Cooldown after damage reduces uptime.","Team repair bonus is wasted if nobody is on generators."],"analysis":["Quick Gambit moves into A because it monetizes chase time directly. If you hold the Killer for thirty or forty seconds while two teammates repair, the perk converts your personal chase skill into teamwide objective pressure without asking those teammates to equip anything.","The Aura component is not filler. Seeing every teammate while chased helps you avoid active generators, healing clusters, or rescue routes, which makes the perk easier to use correctly than a blind repair buff would be.","Its ceiling rises sharply in SWF because the team can deliberately keep strong repairers on generators while the chased Survivor routes elsewhere. Solo Q gets less predictable repair participation, but still benefits from the information layer.","Quick Gambit stays below the elite chase perks because its value disappears when the chase ends quickly or teammates are not repairing. It rewards strong play rather than rescuing weak play, which is powerful but conditional."],"verdict":"A high-skill team perk that turns a good chase into extra generator pressure. Quick Gambit is strongest when the rest of the team is actually repairing while you hold the Killer.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Team"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[55,72],"rankConfidence":"Low","rankStatus":"stable","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Vittorio Toscano"},"synergyPerkIds":["bond","resilience","finesse","windows-of-opportunity"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Bond","Resilience","Finesse","Windows of Opportunity"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Quick Gambit","alternateName":null,"source":"Vittorio Toscano","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While you are being chased by the Killer, reveals the Auras of other Survivors to you and increases those Survivors' Repair speed by 3/4/5%. Quick Gambit enters a 40-second cooldown when you lose a Health State.","activation":["Be in a chase with the Killer.","Ends/deactivates when: The chase-dependent effects end when the chase ends.","Ends/deactivates when: The perk is unavailable for 40 seconds after you lose a Health State."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.2.0): Reduced the cooldown after losing a Health State from 60 seconds to 40 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"During a chase, it shows teammates to you and increases their Generator repair speed until the chase effect ends.","cooldown":"40 seconds after losing a Health State.","duration":["Aura reading and repair bonus: while being chased by the Killer."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Vittorio Toscano","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"breakout","rank":63,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Mobility","Team Support"],"summary":"Near a Killer carrying a teammate, gain Haste while the carried Survivor wiggles 25% faster.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["bodyblock","protection-hit"],"useCases":["Escort a carried teammate toward a difficult hook and accelerate their wiggle progress.","Combine bodyblocks and 10% Haste to lengthen the Killer's route enough for a natural escape.","Coordinate sabotage builds where every extra second of carry time matters."],"counters":["You must remain within only 5 metres of the carrying Killer.","The Killer can hit you, change hook routes, or choose a closer hook.","Without bodyblocks, sabotage, or difficult hook geometry, the wiggle bonus may still be insufficient."],"pros":["Can directly contribute to denying a hook.","Current Haste bonus reaches 10% at Tier III.","Excellent in coordinated carry-save teams."],"cons":["Requires another Survivor to be carried.","Very risky positioning around the Killer.","Low-value in matches where hooks are plentiful and routes are short."],"analysis":["Breakout takes this position because hook denial is one of the largest possible Survivor swings, and the perk contributes in two ways at once. The user moves faster near the carrying Killer while the carried Survivor wiggles 25% faster, improving both escort positioning and the underlying escape timer.","By itself, Breakout rarely guarantees a save. Its real strength appears when combined with bodyblocks, sabotage, awkward hook geometry, or Boil Over. Each delay compounds the accelerated wiggle progress, turning several small inconveniences into a potential escape.","SWF dramatically improves reliability because the team can call pickup locations, coordinate sabotage targets, and decide who is responsible for bodyblocking. Solo Q users often arrive late or discover that the Killer has a clean nearby hook, leaving the perk without enough time to matter.","That opportunity dependence keeps it conditional. Breakout can produce spectacular saves and its 2025 Haste buff improved the escort role, but a general-purpose Survivor build cannot count on the match presenting enough difficult carries to justify the slot."],"verdict":"A strong carry-save specialist. Breakout can help erase a hook when the team builds around it, but it needs coordination and bad hook routes to reach its ceiling.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Carry Save","Team"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Yui Kimura"},"synergyPerkIds":["saboteur","background-player","flashbang","boil-over"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Saboteur","Background Player","Flashbang","Boil Over"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Breakout","alternateName":null,"source":"Yui Kimura","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While within 5 metres of the Killer carrying another Survivor, you gain 6/8/10% Haste and the carried Survivor wiggles 25% faster.","activation":["Killer carries another Survivor.","You are within 5 metres of the Killer.","Ends/deactivates when: Effects end when the carry ends or you leave the range."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.7.0): Increased Haste to 6/8/10%.","plainEnglishSummary":"Staying near the Killer carrying a teammate speeds you up and helps the teammate escape.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Only one Breakout effect applies to a carried Survivor at a time.","statusEffectsInvolved":["Haste"],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Yui Kimura","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"lucky-break","rank":64,"tier":"B","roles":["Stealth","Chase"],"summary":"While Injured, suppress Scratch Marks and Blood for up to 60 seconds, and recharge the timer by healing teammates.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium–High","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["looping","reset"],"useCases":["Break line of sight after taking a hit and deny the Killer the normal Blood and Scratch-Mark trail.","Recharge the timer through productive teammate healing instead of waiting for a cooldown.","Pair with quiet Grunts or silent vaults to make complete chase disappearances more realistic."],"counters":["The timer only runs while you remain Injured and ends when your Health State changes.","A Killer who maintains visual contact does not need Scratch Marks or Blood to follow you.","Aura reading, Killer Instinct, sound, and other tracking methods can bypass the hidden trail."],"pros":["Suppresses two major tracking channels simultaneously.","Long maximum duration at Tier III.","Recharge condition encourages useful teammate healing."],"cons":["Requires an Injured-state chase and a line-of-sight break to realize the strongest value.","Does not hide Grunts of Pain or Aura reads by itself.","Timer can be wasted while running in situations where the Killer already sees you."],"analysis":["Lucky Break rounds out the top fifty because it can make a post-hit chase extraordinarily difficult to track once line of sight is broken. For up to 60 seconds while Injured, both Scratch Marks and Pools of Blood disappear, removing the two trails Killers most commonly use after losing visual contact.","The effect is not automatic chase escape. If you continue running in a straight visible line, the Killer needs no trail. The perk rewards deliberate pathing around walls, elevation, vegetation, and branching routes where the Killer must choose a direction after sight is lost.","Its recharge mechanic is also well designed. Healing another Survivor restores the timer second-for-second, so the player can earn another chase escape window through normal team support. Pairing with Iron Will or Quick & Quiet covers additional tracking channels and makes the stealth package much harder to solve.","Lucky Break stays in B because several Killers have powers or information tools that bypass trail tracking entirely. It also demands that the player recognize and exploit line-of-sight opportunities. In the right chase it can feel oppressive; in a straightforward open pursuit it may accomplish almost nothing."],"verdict":"A strong chase-escape perk for players who know how to vanish after a hit. Lucky Break removes the trail, but you still have to create the moment where the Killer loses sight of you.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Chase Escape","Tracking Denial"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Yui Kimura"},"synergyPerkIds":["iron-will","quick-quiet","overcome","botany-knowledge"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Iron Will","Quick & Quiet","Overcome","Botany Knowledge"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Lucky Break","alternateName":null,"source":"Yui Kimura","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever you are Injured, Lucky Break activates and suppresses the creation of Pools of Blood and Scratch Marks for up to 40/50/60 seconds. While healing another Survivor, it recharges by the time spent healing, up to its initial maximum. It deactivates when its timer runs out or when your Health State changes to anything other than Injured.","activation":["Be in the Injured State.","Ends/deactivates when: The effect ends when its timer runs out or when your Health State changes to anything other than Injured."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (6.1.0): Added one second of timer recharge for every second spent healing another Survivor, up to the initial duration.","plainEnglishSummary":"While Injured, it hides Blood Pools and Scratch Marks for a limited timer that you can refill by healing someone else.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Suppression timer: up to 40/50/60 seconds by tier; time spent healing another Survivor restores the timer one-for-one up to its initial maximum."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Healing another Survivor recharges the timer by the same amount of time spent healing, capped at the perk's initial duration."],"sourceCharacter":"Yui Kimura","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"road-life","rank":65,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Skill Check","Self-Sustain"],"summary":"While injured on a Generator, earn Tokens from Great basic Skill Checks; at the threshold, spend them to self-heal 10% faster.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["health-state","reset"],"useCases":["Convert productive injured Generator repair into access to a repeatable self-heal.","Stay productive while charging the perk instead of spending time on a separate setup objective.","Use it when independent self-reset access is more valuable than carrying a dedicated healing perk or item."],"counters":["Token acquisition depends on Great basic Skill Check frequency and execution, so charge time varies substantially.","Missed checks cost progress, and the practical effect of interruptions still needs controlled testing.","Stake Out is not a partner: its special Skill Checks replace the basic checks Road Life needs while Tokens are held."],"pros":["The completed self-heal is fast enough to be meaningful.","The perk charges during productive Generator work.","Live gameplay supports repeatable use rather than a one-use payoff."],"cons":["The Token economy is still unmeasured and is the main reason the exact rank is provisional.","Requires staying injured while repairing to build toward the heal.","Great-check consistency matters."],"analysis":["Road Life is best understood as a self-heal access perk whose reward is strong once earned. Live gameplay showed the completed heal is practically useful and can be earned again, so the old one-use and 100%-speed framing is obsolete.","The unresolved variable is the Token economy. The precision review could not justify the optimistic charge-rate assumption behind rank #58, so the perk moved to #65 with a wide credible range.","A neutral working assumption is roughly one activation per generator's worth of injured repair for a player who hits most Great checks. That is an assumption to test, not a mechanic to encode as fact.","Because setup happens during productive repair, Road Life still compares favorably with slower or travel-dependent self-heal options even when its charge time is imperfect."],"verdict":"A genuinely useful self-heal once charged, held to a provisional mid-B rank because the real Token-acquisition rate is still the unanswered question.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:audit-explicit"],"tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[45,95],"rankConfidence":"Low","rankStatus":"provisional","evidenceStatus":"needs-controlled-testing","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Vee Boonyasak"},"synergyPerkIds":["hyperfocus","one-two-three-four","botany-knowledge","resilience"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":["stake-out"],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Hyperfocus","One-Two-Three-Four!","Botany Knowledge","Resilience"],"antiSynergies":["Stake Out"],"name":"Road Life","alternateName":null,"source":"Vee Boonyasak","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While injured and repairing a Generator, hitting a basic Great Skill Check gives 1 Token and missing a basic Skill Check removes 1 Token. At 6/5/4 Tokens, you can heal yourself; spending all Tokens lets you self-heal 10% faster. After you stop healing, this self-heal effect ends after 4 seconds.","activation":["Be Injured and repairing a Generator to gain or lose Tokens from basic Repair Skill Checks.","Reach 6/5/4 Tokens to gain the ability to self-heal.","Begin self-healing to spend all Tokens and receive the 10% self-heal speed bonus.","Ends/deactivates when: Stopping the self-heal starts a 4-second grace period; after 4 seconds the granted self-heal effect ends.","Ends/deactivates when: Missed basic Repair Skill Checks remove 1 Token while the token-building condition is active."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Reworked into a Repair-Skill-Check token system that grants self-healing at 6/5/4 Tokens, spends all Tokens on use, gives 10% faster self-healing, and ends 4 seconds after healing stops.","plainEnglishSummary":"While injured on Generators, Great checks build and missed checks remove tokens; reaching the tier threshold lets you spend them to self-heal slightly faster.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Granted self-heal ability persists for 4 seconds after stopping the heal before ending."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"While Injured and repairing, basic Great Skill Checks add 1 Token and missed basic Skill Checks remove 1. Threshold is 6/5/4 by tier. Starting the granted self-heal spends all Tokens.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The final live self-heal speed bonus is 10%, not the higher PTB test value."],"sourceCharacter":"Vee Boonyasak","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"lightweight","rank":66,"tier":"B","roles":["Stealth","Chase"],"summary":"Make Scratch Marks disappear 5 seconds sooner at Tier III and spawn in much less consistent patches.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["looping"],"useCases":["Make ordinary chase pathing harder to read after line-of-sight breaks.","Reduce the reliability of Scratch Marks during indoor-map rotations and dense tiles.","Pair passive trail disruption with stronger sound or Aura-denial tools."],"counters":["Killers who maintain direct visual contact do not need Scratch Marks.","Aura reading, Killer Instinct, Blood, and Grunts of Pain remain available tracking channels.","The effect is subtle and may not create a meaningful misread on open terrain."],"pros":["Always active with no trigger or cooldown.","Reduces both duration and consistency of Scratch Marks.","Easy to equip without changing how the rest of the build functions."],"cons":["Indirect value that depends on the Killer losing sight of you.","Does not hide other tracking information.","Hard to measure and less reliable than complete Scratch-Mark suppression."],"analysis":["Lightweight opens the second fifty at this position because passive tracking disruption has real value without asking for any setup. Scratch Marks disappear five seconds sooner at Tier III and spawn in less consistent patches, so Killers receive a noisier trail whenever they lose direct visual contact.","The perk is especially useful on indoor maps and structures with frequent corners. A Killer who briefly loses sight may expect a full trail through the next doorway and instead find scattered or already-fading information. That hesitation can buy just enough time for a Survivor to change floors, double back, or reach another tile.","Lightweight also has a forgiving floor. Unlike Lucky Break or Quick & Quiet, the player does not need to be Injured, vault at the right moment, or watch a cooldown. It simply modifies every sprint trail in the Trial. That makes it useful for players who want stealth value without dedicating attention to an activation condition.","Its ceiling is limited because the perk never fully removes Scratch Marks and does nothing to Grunts, Blood, Auras, or powers that reveal Survivors directly. Strong Killers who keep visual contact may barely notice it. The perk is consistently present, but the size of its payoff is highly situational."],"verdict":"A reliable passive tracking-disruption perk. Lightweight will not make you invisible, but it makes every line-of-sight break slightly harder for the Killer to solve.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Chase Escape","Tracking Denial"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"general","sourceCharacter":"General"},"synergyPerkIds":["iron-will","fixated","quick-quiet","lucky-break"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Iron Will","Fixated","Quick & Quiet","Lucky Break"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Lightweight","alternateName":null,"source":"General perk","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Reduces the lifetime of your Scratch Marks by 3/4/5 seconds. It also reduces the spawn chance of patches of Scratch Marks by 60%, making their spacing inconsistent.","activation":[],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (6.1.0): Increased Scratch Mark lifetime reduction from 1/2/3 to 3/4/5 seconds and added a 60% patch-spawn chance reduction effect.","plainEnglishSummary":"Your Scratch Marks disappear sooner and spawn in less consistent patches.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Applies to Scratch Marks whenever they are created; lifetime reduction is 3/4/5 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"General","isGeneralPerk":true,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"autodidact","rank":67,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Skill Check","Utility"],"summary":"Healing Skill Checks build Tokens that turn later Good checks into enormous healing bursts, eventually reaching +60% progression at five Tokens.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["reset","health-state"],"useCases":["Turn repeated teammate heals into increasingly explosive healing Skill Checks.","Recover a heavily injured team quickly once several Tokens have been earned.","Pair with effects that increase healing Skill Check frequency to reach the high-token state sooner."],"counters":["The first Skill Check starts with a 15% progression penalty.","Token gain depends on actually receiving healing Skill Checks.","The perk is inactive when healing with a Med-Kit."],"pros":["Very high healing ceiling at maximum Tokens.","Tokens persist and reward continued support play through the Trial.","Late-game Skill Checks can remove huge chunks of a heal instantly."],"cons":["Unreliable early game and vulnerable to poor Skill Check RNG.","Initial penalty can actively slow the first heals.","Requires repeated teammate healing to reach its best state."],"analysis":["Autodidact takes this position because few healing perks have such a dramatic gap between their opening and fully stacked states. At zero Tokens, a Skill Check actually loses 15% healing progress. At five Tokens, a successful check grants an enormous +60%, allowing one proc to erase most of the remaining heal.","The challenge is getting there. Tokens only arrive when healing Skill Checks occur, and the game does not promise them on demand. A fast early heal may complete before the perk generates meaningful stacks, leaving Autodidact worse than an empty perk slot for that interaction.","Once several Tokens are banked, the equation changes. Multi-injury situations become much easier to stabilize, and Empathy helps the user actively seek injured teammates to create more opportunities. One-Two-Three-Four! can also increase Skill Check frequency, making the stack-building phase less dependent on luck.","Autodidact sits in B rather than A because the first half of its progression is too inconsistent. A perk whose ceiling can be spectacular but whose floor can literally subtract healing progress needs that volatility reflected in the ranking."],"verdict":"A volatile healing engine that starts badly and can end brilliantly. Autodidact rewards dedicated support play, but Skill Check RNG prevents it from being a dependable top-tier option.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["High Ceiling"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Adam Francis"},"synergyPerkIds":["empathy","one-two-three-four","botany-knowledge","solidarity"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Empathy","One-Two-Three-Four!","Botany Knowledge","Solidarity"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Autodidact","alternateName":null,"source":"Adam Francis","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While healing another Survivor without a Med-Kit, successful Healing Skill Checks grant 1 Token up to 3/4/5. Great Skill Checks cannot occur. Each Token improves Skill Check progression by 15 percentage points, starting at a 15% penalty with zero Tokens (then 0%, +15%, +30%, +45%, +60% as applicable).","activation":["Heal another Survivor without a Med-Kit.","Complete a Healing Skill Check to gain a Token.","Ends/deactivates when: Does not activate while healing with a Med-Kit."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.1.0): Reduced the initial Healing Skill Check progression penalty to -15%.","plainEnglishSummary":"Healing Skill Checks build tokens that improve later check progress, while Great Skill Checks are suppressed.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Gain 1 Token per successful Healing Skill Check; tier caps are 3/4/5; Tokens persist for the Trial.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Great Healing Skill Checks are suppressed."],"sourceCharacter":"Adam Francis","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"soul-guard","rank":68,"tier":"B","roles":["Anti-Slug","Recovery"],"summary":"After being healed or recovering from the Dying State, gain brief Endurance; while Cursed, you can also fully self-recover from the ground.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["dying-state","endurance","anti-slug","conspicuous-action"],"useCases":["Prevent an immediate re-down after a teammate or perk gets you off the ground.","Pair with Conviction or Unbreakable so a self-pick has a protected escape window.","Exploit the unlimited self-recovery clause in matches where you are Cursed."],"counters":["Endurance only lasts up to 8 seconds and is cancelled by a Conspicuous Action.","The normal Endurance trigger requires first getting out of the Dying State.","The Cursed self-recovery clause depends on a Hex-related condition the Survivor does not fully control."],"pros":["Protects the vulnerable moment immediately after a ground recovery.","Excellent synergy with several strong anti-slug perks.","Can become dramatically stronger in Cursed matches."],"cons":["Provides no value before a Dying-State recovery occurs.","Short protection window.","Part of its ceiling depends on the Killer bringing a relevant Hex effect."],"analysis":["Soul Guard ranks this position because getting off the ground is not always enough. A Killer can immediately hit a freshly recovered Survivor and erase the entire rescue. Soul Guard adds up to eight seconds of Endurance after the recovery, forcing the Killer to respect that brief protection window.","The perk has become especially relevant alongside Conviction. Conviction creates a temporary self-pick, while Soul Guard can protect the first hit after standing. Unbreakable and Boon: Exponential create similar combinations. In those builds, Soul Guard acts as the safety layer that turns recovery into actual movement rather than an instant re-down.","The Cursed clause can be extraordinary but should not dominate the ranking. When active, full self-recovery becomes available without the usual one-use restriction, but Survivors cannot rely on every Killer bringing a Hex that places them in the relevant state. We treat that as upside rather than baseline value.","Soul Guard remains B because its activation is reactive and specific. Matches without meaningful slugging can leave it nearly invisible. In slug-heavy matches, however, it is one of the best support pieces for a recovery-focused build."],"verdict":"A strong anti-slug companion perk. Soul Guard is most valuable when another effect already gets you off the ground and you need protection long enough to actually escape.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Endurance"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Cheryl Mason"},"synergyPerkIds":["conviction","unbreakable","plot-twist","boon-exponential"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Conviction","Unbreakable","Plot Twist","Boon: Exponential"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Soul Guard","alternateName":null,"source":"Cheryl Mason","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever you heal or recover from the Dying State, gain Endurance for 4/6/8 seconds. Endurance is cancelled early if you perform a Conspicuous Action. This effect has a 30-second cooldown. While Cursed, you can fully recover from the Dying State using Self-Recovery.","activation":["Heal or recover from the Dying State to trigger Endurance.","Be Cursed by a Hex effect to unlock Self-Recovery from the Dying State.","Ends/deactivates when: Endurance ends after 4/6/8 seconds or early after a Conspicuous Action.","Ends/deactivates when: Self-Recovery from Dying is available only while Cursed."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (4.7.0): Added a 30-second cooldown between Endurance activations.","plainEnglishSummary":"Healing or recovering grants brief Endurance, and being affected by a Hex lets you fully recover from the Dying State.","cooldown":"30 seconds between Endurance activations","duration":["Endurance: 4/6/8 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Endurance","Cursed"],"specialInteractions":["The self-recovery effect is conditional on being affected by a Hex; the Endurance trigger has a separate 30-second cooldown."],"sourceCharacter":"Cheryl Mason","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"friendly-competition","rank":69,"tier":"B","roles":["Objective","Team Support"],"summary":"Finish a Generator cooperatively and every finisher repairs 10% faster for up to 90 seconds afterward.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["pressure","swf"],"useCases":["Carry a cooperative generator completion into faster work on the next objective.","Buff multiple Survivors from one successful co-op finish.","Coordinate a SWF split after completion so several generators benefit from the same 10% bonus."],"counters":["Requires completing a generator cooperatively.","The perk does nothing before that first qualifying completion.","Ten percent is useful but not enough to justify inefficiently stacking generators just to trigger it."],"pros":["Long 80/85/90-second duration.","Can buff several Survivors simultaneously.","Rewards a common objective event rather than a niche side task."],"cons":["Activation requires co-op completion.","Can tempt players into unnecessary generator stacking.","No direct chase or rescue value."],"analysis":["Friendly Competition doubled its repair bonus in 10.2 from 5% to 10%, while shortening the duration to 80/85/90 seconds. That trade strongly favors the perk because the bonus is large enough to shape the next objective rather than merely decorate it.","The correct macro remains “finish together, then split.” Every participating Survivor carries the buff away from the completed generator, so coordinated teams can turn one co-op finish into pressure on several different objectives.","The activation still creates a risk of over-stacking. Survivors should not crowd a generator solely to trigger the perk when separate repairs would have been stronger.","At 10%, however, the payoff is now substantial enough to justify a serious re-rank. The old 5% evaluation understates the live version."],"verdict":"A real objective snowball perk after the 10.2 buff. Finish one generator together, then spread the 10% bonus across the map.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"tags":["Co-op","Team"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Thalita Lyra"},"synergyPerkIds":["prove-thyself","deja-vu","teamwork-full-circuit","hyperfocus"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Prove Thyself","Déjà Vu","Teamwork: Full Circuit","Hyperfocus"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Friendly Competition","alternateName":null,"source":"Thalita Lyra","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever you finish repairing a Generator with at least 1 other Survivor, the Survivors who finished repairing it repair 10% faster for 80/85/90 seconds.","activation":["You must complete a Generator while at least one other Survivor is also repairing it.","Ends/deactivates when: Each affected Survivor's repair-speed bonus expires after 80/85/90 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Increased cooperative repair bonus from 5% to 10% and reduced its duration from 100/110/120 to 80/85/90 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"Completing a Generator cooperatively gives all finishing participants a 10% repair-speed bonus for a tiered duration.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Repair-speed bonus: 80/85/90 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The repair-speed bonus affects every Survivor who participated in that Generator's repair, including the perk user."],"sourceCharacter":"Thalita Lyra","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"overcome","rank":70,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Exhaustion","Mobility"],"summary":"When a Healthy hit injures you, extend the normal on-hit sprint by 2 additional seconds, then become Exhausted.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["exhausted","haste","looping"],"useCases":["Turn the first hit of a chase into enough distance to reach a much stronger tile.","Escape weak map areas after being caught away from resources.","Pair the long post-hit sprint with tracking denial so the Killer loses the follow-up chase."],"counters":["It only triggers when going from Healthy to Injured.","Exposed downs, one-shot powers, and already being Injured prevent normal activation.","It cannot be used while Exhausted."],"pros":["Very easy to activate in ordinary basic-hit chases.","Two extra sprint seconds create a large amount of raw distance.","Low mechanical burden compared with timing-based Exhaustion perks."],"cons":["Requires entering chase Healthy.","Poor against Killers that frequently down without a normal Healthy-to-Injured hit.","Provides less tactical control than Sprint Burst or Lithe."],"analysis":["Overcome takes this position because two extra seconds of on-hit sprint is a great deal of distance for almost no execution requirement. If a standard Killer lands the first hit, the Survivor can often leave a weak area entirely and reach a stronger structure before the chase resumes.","The perk is especially friendly to players who dislike managing Sprint Burst or landing Dead Hard timing. There is no button to press and no vault to find. The downside is equally simple: the correct health-state transition must occur. If you begin Injured or are downed in one hit, Overcome does nothing.","Tracking-denial pairings raise its ceiling. Lucky Break can erase the trail during the extended sprint, and Iron Will reduces sound afterward. The combination can transform raw distance into a complete chase loss if the Survivor reaches a strong line-of-sight break.","Overcome stays below the top Exhaustion perks because it gives the Killer control over the trigger and requires a Healthy state. Its ease of use and strong distance still make it a very respectable chase perk."],"verdict":"One of the easiest ways to turn a first hit into major distance. Overcome is strong and forgiving, but health-state dependence makes it less universal than the best Exhaustion perks.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Jonah Vasquez"},"synergyPerkIds":["lucky-break","iron-will","botany-knowledge","resurgence"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Lucky Break","Iron Will","Botany Knowledge","Resurgence"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Overcome","alternateName":null,"source":"Jonah Vasquez","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"When you enter the Injured State from full health, Overcome extends the duration of the resulting On-hit Sprint boost by 2 seconds. It cannot be used while you are Exhausted, and it causes Exhausted for 60/50/40 seconds by tier.","activation":["Be at full health and enter the Injured State.","Not be Exhausted when the hit occurs.","Ends/deactivates when: The extension applies only to the On-hit Sprint from the qualifying health-state loss.","Ends/deactivates when: The perk cannot activate while Exhausted; the Exhausted status prevents its use until it expires or is removed."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified after the perk's introduction; later tracked entry is wording standardization, and the official 5.4.0 Dying-State change was a bug fix.","plainEnglishSummary":"Taking a hit from full health extends the resulting sprint burst by 2 seconds and causes tier-scaled Exhaustion.","cooldown":null,"duration":["On-hit Sprint boost: extended by 2 seconds beyond its normal duration.","Exhausted: 60/50/40 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Exhausted"],"specialInteractions":["The trigger is specifically entering the Injured State from full health; the official 5.4.0 notes fixed a bug that had also allowed activation when entering the Dying State."],"sourceCharacter":"Jonah Vasquez","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"empathy","rank":71,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Healing","Team Support"],"summary":"See injured or dying teammates at extremely long range, reaching 128 metres at Tier III.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":4,"swf":2,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","solo-q","dying-state"],"useCases":["Locate injured teammates for healing without wasting time searching.","Infer where a chase is happening by watching an injured Survivor's movement.","Track downed teammates and decide whether a pickup or rescue route is developing."],"counters":["Healthy teammates are not shown.","The perk reveals teammate state and position, not the Killer directly.","SWF voice communication can reproduce some of the information."],"pros":["Enormous effective range.","Excellent for dedicated healing/support builds.","Provides useful indirect chase information in Solo Q."],"cons":["No information about Healthy Survivors.","Does not directly accelerate any action.","Lower marginal value in coordinated teams."],"analysis":["Empathy ranks this position because 128 metres is effectively map-wide on many Trials. Whenever a teammate is Injured or Dying, their Aura becomes a persistent information source that tells you where support is needed and often where Killer pressure is happening.","Dedicated healers get the clearest value. Autodidact, Botany Knowledge, and For the People all become easier to use when the player can immediately locate the next injured teammate instead of searching. The perk therefore turns information into action more naturally than many generic Aura perks.","Solo Q also benefits from chase inference. An injured Survivor sprinting across the far side of the map is often the current chase target, which can tell you that your generator is safe. A suddenly downed Aura warns you that a pickup or slug scenario is developing.","Empathy remains B because Healthy teammates are invisible and the perk itself changes no speed or health state. Bond is more generally useful at close range, while Empathy is better when the user specifically wants global information about injured players."],"verdict":"A superb support-information perk with near-global range. Empathy is strongest when your build has a reason to actively seek injured teammates.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Support"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Claudette Morel"},"synergyPerkIds":["autodidact","botany-knowledge","well-make-it","for-the-people"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"synergies":["Autodidact","Botany Knowledge","We'll Make It","For the People"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Empathy","alternateName":null,"source":"Claudette Morel","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"The Auras of injured or dying Survivors are revealed to you within 64/96/128 metres.","activation":["An injured or dying Survivor must be within the applicable Aura-reading range.","Ends/deactivates when: The Aura reveal ends when the Survivor is no longer injured or dying or moves out of range."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (2.6.0): Changed the Aura-reading range to 64/96/128 m from an effectively unlimited 32/64/99999.99 m range.","plainEnglishSummary":"You see injured and dying teammates' Auras when they are within your tier's range.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Claudette Morel","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"wiretap","rank":72,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Objective"],"summary":"After enough generator repair, bug a generator so all Survivors can see the Killer's Aura whenever they come within 14 metres of it.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","pressure"],"useCases":["Turn a central or contested generator into a local Killer-detection beacon.","Use the Aura zone during nearby chases to see the Killer through walls and structures.","Give every teammate information from one placed device."],"counters":["The perk requires 40% total personal generator repair to charge.","Damaging the bugged generator deactivates the device.","Poor generator placement can create an Aura zone that nobody uses."],"pros":["Teamwide information rather than owner-only Aura reading.","Long device duration at Tier III.","Can be extremely strong around central indoor generators or chase structures."],"cons":["Needs repair setup and a strategically useful generator.","Killer can remove it by damaging the generator.","Limited 14-metre detection radius."],"analysis":["Wiretap takes this position because it turns generator work into a reusable team information zone. After enough repair contribution, the Survivor can install the device on a generator, and every teammate sees the Killer's Aura whenever they enter the nearby radius.","The perk is particularly strong around central generators and indoor structures. A loop that passes near the bugged objective effectively gains intermittent wallhacks, making Killer mindgames much harder. Even Survivors elsewhere can use the Aura appearance to understand where pressure currently sits.","Placement quality determines most of the value. A safe corner generator the Killer never revisits is a poor target, while a contested central objective can produce repeated reads. The device also disappears when the Killer damages the generator, so obvious placements may have short lives.","Wiretap is held back because it requires both charge and geography. When the setup is right it can produce teamwide information approaching premium information quality, but that setup is too variable for a higher general ranking."],"verdict":"A strong local information beacon when placed intelligently. Wiretap can give an entire team repeated Killer Aura reads, but only around the right generator.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Aura Reading"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Ada Wong"},"synergyPerkIds":["deja-vu","open-handed","kindred","troubleshooter"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Déjà Vu","Open-Handed","Kindred","Troubleshooter"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Wiretap","alternateName":null,"source":"Ada Wong","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After you repair Generators for a total of 40% progression, Wiretap activates. While active, use the Active Ability button while standing next to a Generator to install a listening device for 100/110/120 seconds. All Survivors see the Killer's Aura when the Killer comes within 14 m of that Generator. The device deactivates when its timer expires or when the Generator is damaged; all Survivors see the Aura of a bugged Generator in yellow.","activation":["Repair Generators for a total of 40% progression to activate the perk.","While active, stand next to a Generator and use the Active Ability button to install the device.","Ends/deactivates when: The device ends after 100/110/120 seconds or when the Generator is damaged."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified from available patch history.","plainEnglishSummary":"After repairing 40% total Generator progress, you can attach a device that shares the Killer's Aura when they approach a Generator.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Device duration: 100/110/120 seconds, unless the Generator is damaged first."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Any effects that change the perk user's Repair speed also affect how quickly Wiretap charges.","The Aura-reveal effect remains active while the Generator is blocked by the Entity."],"sourceCharacter":"Ada Wong","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"}]);
